WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.960
and I'd like to welcome you to the Joy of Painting.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.600
This is an instructional guide designed to take you

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.020
through the major components of the different paintings

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.560
that we've done in the television series.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.080
In this instructional guide, we'll try to take you

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.860
step by step through the different aspects of paintings.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.460
We'll go through trees, mountains, water, skies,

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.160
all the different components that make up paintings.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.710
And before we get started, let me talk just a second

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.350
about the equipment that we're gonna be using.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.960
We're gonna be using a two inch and a one inch brush.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.970
Now these two brushes will be

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.760
the major brushes that we'll use

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.580
to do the different parts of these paintings.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.470
We have a couple of knives here.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.180
We have a large and a small knife.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.520
Now these two knives we'll use over and over and over.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.860
I think you'll find that they're fantastic pieces of equipment.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.390
We'll use a couple of fan brushes,

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.610
a number three and a number six fan brush.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:21.510
With these two brushes,

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.770
we can do just about everything that we need to do.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.040
A script liner brush.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.710
This brush is used for doing, oh, fine detail.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.720
probably the most important part of the painting,

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:32.680
the signature.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:37.860
Okay, and then also, we will use a one inch round brush.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.530
And I'll show you how to use this fantastic brush

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.130
and make some beautiful effects with it.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:44.970
Alrighty, before we get started,

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:46.730
I'm gonna have them put a supply list up

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.720
that'll give you all the materials that you need

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.700
to complete these projects with me.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.460
And I'll be back with you in just a second.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.390
Alright, I think we're about ready to get started here.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.290
Now before we get started, let me show you

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.650
a couple more little items that I think

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.030
will be very helpful to you.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.360
First of all, you know on the television shows

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.520
I beat the brush on the ladder

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.670
and paint thinner goes all over the place.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:04:59.880
If you want to contain,

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.440
that here's a simple device that will really

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:03.960
save you a lot of problems.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.460
This is a brush beater rack, and this rack

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.220
fits in the bottom of a waste paper basket,

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.970
and you shake the brush inside of the basket,

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.630
and then you beat the devil with all the bristles

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:15.170
right on this, and that will really keep you

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.150
from covering your whole living room

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:20.540
or whichever room you're painting in with paint.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:24.360
Alrighty, next thing you need here is a big pallet.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.450
You really need a large area to work.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.810
When you're using these large brushes,

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.960
a big pallet, oh, it...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.140
it's worth its weight in gold.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:33.860
And I like a palette that's made out of a clear acrylic.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.070
That's very smooth, easy to load your knife and brushes,

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:38.810
easy to clean, lightweight,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.800
and I think you'll find that great.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.070
Alright, let's get started here.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.110
We'll take the old two-inch brush,

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.850
and I've already covered this canvas

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.490
with a thin, even coat of liquid white.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:52.270
And all you're looking for is just a very, very thin coat.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.940
When you touch it, it should just cover your finger.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.980
You should still be able to see your finger through there.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:05:59.780
It shouldn't be real.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:01.730
heavy on there, just a little bit.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.510
Of course, then you end up with fingers

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:04.870
that have white spots on the end.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:10.080
Alrighty, on this canvas, this is a 24 by 30 inch canvas,

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.440
I'm gonna take and just make several different types

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.220
of skies and let you see how they're made

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.660
and hope you'll enjoy it.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.780
Let's start today with a little bit of phthalo blue.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:21.600
And to load the brush, just tap it.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.370
Pull out a little bit of color,

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.630
little bit of color, just like so, and then tap it.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.760
That assures a nice even distribution.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.740
of color all the way through the bristles, see there?

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.260
That's very important, you don't wanna get

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.680
great big streaks in your sky.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:36.560
Alright, let's go up here.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.460
Probably the easiest sky to make

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.910
is just by taking and making little criss-cross,

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.380
little criss-cross strokes, and just let the brush

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.920
sorta bounce around, tiny little criss-cross strokes.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.500
Don't get too big here, see?

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.120
Just let it bounce around, and leave some holes up here.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.480
There we go, just like so.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:02.820
Leave a few holes in.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:06.000
And as you work downward, it's picking up the liquid white

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.580
and automatically it gets lighter toward the horizon.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.020
That's what we're looking for.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.380
Okay, let me clean the brush.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.620
Now we clean our brushes with odorless thinner.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:17.820
And I really, really recommend you use odorless thinner.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:19.080
You're gonna be working by yourself.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:25.930
Shake it off and just beat the devil out of it.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:28.770
This is when the brush beater rack will save your marriage.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:29.980
Okay, let's go back.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.870
back up here now, very lightly,

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.260
start in the light area and work upward.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.210
We'll blend this together.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.630
We don't want to blend it so firmly

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:39.310
that we lose these little light areas.

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:40.350
We're trying to save those.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.920
They'll turn out to be the pretty parts of your sky.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.780
You can actually make it look like clouds

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:47.760
without painting anything at all in it.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:52.850
See there, just like so.

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:55.230
And that easy, you have one of the simplest,

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:57.010
most basic types of skies.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:58.850
That easy.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.540
And that's all there is to it.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.360
Okay, let me show you another one real quick here.

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.190
For this one, we'll use a one-inch brush.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.460
And, I'll tell you what, I'll use Prussian blue this time.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:15.400
It's a little darker, and I'm gonna put some clouds

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:16.780
in this one, so we need a darker color

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.330
to make it really stand out.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.350
But I'm loading the brush the same way.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:22.070
Just tap it into a little bit of color.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:24.810
This is a very, very strong color.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:25.770
Let's go up to the canvas.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:28.720
And maybe in this sky, watch here.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:29.960
Take and...

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.760
Make little, tiny, happy circles, see them?

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.660
Really, keep that brush moving, keep it moving,

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.060
keep it moving, don't let it stop.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:45.040
All kinds of little circles, keep it moving, keep it moving.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.680
You want areas where the paint's thick,

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:50.120
areas where it's thin, areas where there's no paint at all.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:54.000
It's most important, just keep that son of a gun

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.110
moving continually, just like that.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:00.790
Okay, good.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:05.110
Now then, I'm gonna take a clean, dry, two inch brush,

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:09.720
and I'm gonna very gently begin blending this.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.740
Actually, what I'm doing here is pulling a little bit

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.400
of that color into the light area.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.470
Just little tiny circles.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.390
And notice, I'll exaggerate it here.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.730
See, you're using just the top corner of the brush.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.170
It's almost a natural tendency to want to use

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:26.170
the bottom like this.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.970
If you use the bottom of the brush,

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:29.980
you have no way of...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.420
of telling where it's hitting, use the top corner

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:35.320
and you can see exactly where it's hitting on that cloud.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.960
Okay, there we go.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.880
Now, we just mix this up a little bit, how easy that is.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.990
It's mixing with the liquid white

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:46.960
and all these beautiful effects just happen.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:51.340
And then very lightly, you can just blend all this together.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.210
Just blend it, blend it, blend it.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.370
Now your sky would be finished right there.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.980
This is a super way of making a real

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.420
real rough sky like there's a big storm coming in.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.900
It's very nice for winter scenes.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:06.480
If I was doing a winter scene,

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.630
I would add a little bit of black to it and gray it down.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:13.720
Okay now watch, let me get another one inch brush.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.580
I'm gonna go right into some titanium white.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:19.460
I had a little touch of bright red to that,

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:22.910
just a little touch, little touch, it's very strong.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.560
Pull that brush in one direction,

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.440
load a lot of color into it.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.890
Look at that brush, see?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.180
There's a lot of paint in there, look at the end of it.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.660
Ooh, a lot of paint, let's go up here.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.370
Okay, now then, if you want to lay some clouds in here,

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.340
come in here in these light areas and watch,

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:46.600
make tiny little circles, still making the little circles.

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:49.860
Keep the brush moving, I can't say that enough times.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.780
Keep that son of a gun just moving on the canvas.

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:56.000
If you don't, you're gonna end up with

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.260
great big cotton balls up in the sky.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.140
There, you can just lay in cloud after cloud,

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:05.160
as many of them as you want.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.680
This is your world, this piece of canvas,

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:10.390
so you do whatever makes you happy on here.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.460
Everybody sees nature different,

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:16.060
everybody sees skies different.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:20.750
Now, back to two-inch brush,

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.030
and if you just have a little bit of paint on your brush,

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:26.590
you can usually just beat that little son of a gun,

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:29.320
and that way it'll take out the little bit of paint.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:29.980
If you have a lot of paint,

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.580
paint on your brush, then you're gonna have

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:32.740
to wash the brush, okay?

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:33.780
Let's go back up here now.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:38.130
Very gently, still using the top corner of the brush,

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:41.440
blend the bottom only of these white clouds out.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.660
Just the bottom, and very gently, very gently,

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.210
very gently, very gently.

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:52.170
Tiny little circles, still using just the top corner

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:57.660
of the brush, give it another wrap,

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.780
just take the paint off, then lift upward.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.920
Fluff that cloud, fluff it, look it there.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:07.000
Fluff it, fluff it, there we go.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:10.580
And when you do that, you're gonna pull

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:11.860
these little stringy things out.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:12.700
Don't worry about them.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:15.570
It's what makes your cloud look soft when it's over.

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:20.400
And very lightly, very lightly, just grazing the canvas.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.800
You just caress the canvas.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:26.650
Just go across it, that easy.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.830
You have a fantastic sky, beautiful.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:33.890
clouds, but you see how you can change the mood of this.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.690
It started off look like a big stormy sky,

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.510
and that easy, it turns into a happy little sky.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.090
It's a bright day, makes you feel good to look at it.

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:44.950
Alright, let's do a different kind now.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:47.720
Tell you what, let's do here.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.420
We'll go right into some of the,

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.500
we'll use the Prussian blue again.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:55.690
It's a nice, strong blue.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:58.320
Let's go right up here, alright.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:02.080
I'll just lay in a little sky here.

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:05.250
Even if I cover up some of this other than we did here,

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:06.870
it's no big deal, you've seen how to make it,

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:08.150
and you know how to do it now.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.560
Starting at the top, working down.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.220
Once again, so the top of the sky

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:16.780
is darker than the bottom.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.740
That helps create the illusion of distance in your painting.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:29.300
I'm gonna wash the brush, shake it off, there we go.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:34.020
Alright, tell you what, this time, let's use the fan brush.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:37.100
And I'm gonna load this brush by pulling it

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:38.820
through some titanium white.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.320
We'll add some bright red to that too.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:47.580
There we go, there we go.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:51.860
Just a lot of paint in the bristles, look right here.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:54.330
Look at all the paint that's in those bristles.

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:58.460
Let's go up here.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:13:59.360
Now,

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.890
Right up in here, we'll make a happy little cloud.

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:03.670
Use just the corner of the brush,

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:05.820
and take the corner of that brush,

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:08.590
and make tiny little circles.

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:11.320
Now these, you can make more delicate clouds

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:12.440
than we did with a larger brush.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.880
Use the other side here, see there?

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:18.310
This is where you can make all kinds of little shapes,

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:28.250
and little fluffy things, and do these in layers.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.750
Now watch, top corner of the brush again,

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:35.230
and just barely touching.

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.270
You wanna blend the bottom of this cloud out,

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.020
but don't touch the top at all yet.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:42.800
Don't touch the top at all.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:46.040
Now, same as before, grab this and fluff it up.

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:49.030
Look at all the beautiful little things that happen there.

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:53.730
And then very lightly, very lightly, just go across it.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.620
Okay, now then, a little bit more of the bright red.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.980
I'm loading this brush back up again.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:04.660
Now maybe there's layers of clouds here.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:06.780
Do one layer at a time.

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:09.460
Finish this cloud completely before you start this one.

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:11.980
There we go.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.860
Now we can put another cloud right here.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:19.030
You can just put as many layers of clouds

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:20.150
in your world as you want.

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.400
But one layer at a time.

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:27.130
With a large brush, all we're gonna do

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:29.140
is blend the base of it out.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.670
Blend it out, blend it out, okay?

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:34.650
Then we'll fluff it.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:39.080
And this fluffing is done in big circular patterns,

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:40.060
big circles.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:45.010
If you go straight up, it'll look like it's raining up.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:47.420
See there?

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:50.880
And you can just go on and on and on.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.360
You could take a little more paint here,

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.840
and drop in another happy little cloud.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:59.700
Just as many clouds as you want.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.950
See, you can make little stringy ones down here.

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:10.330
There's really no limit to this.

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:12.610
You can fill up your whole canvas with nothing but clouds,

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:13.990
and that's not bad.

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:15.470
That's a super way to practice.

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:24.360
And up, and gently, gently blend it.

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:27.140
This blending across removes the brush strokes

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.400
and puts it all together.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:29.960
