you can take and blend all of this.

00:30:51.660 --> 00:30:53.420
Hmm, isn't that something?

00:30:54.410 --> 00:30:59.960
That's a super easy way to make a very effective little sun.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:08.340
Alright, I think with that we have about six different skies.

00:31:08.580 --> 00:31:11.720
This will give you a nice selection of skies

00:31:11.720 --> 00:31:14.500
that you can make many, many fantastic paintings.

00:31:14.800 --> 00:31:18.020
I'm gonna change canvases and I'll be back with you in just a second.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.580
Welcome back, glad you could join me again.

00:31:32.100 --> 00:31:35.020
Already, we've got another canvas up here and we're ready to go.

00:31:35.100 --> 00:31:36.320
Now I've already covered this canvas

00:31:36.320 --> 00:31:38.080
with a thin even coat of the liquid white,

00:31:38.280 --> 00:31:40.900
and on top of that I've taken just a little bit of phthalo blue

00:31:40.900 --> 00:31:43.100
and dropped in a few little areas here and there

00:31:43.100 --> 00:31:45.670
just to break up the monotony of it being all white.

00:31:46.010 --> 00:31:48.000
And in this segment, we're gonna practice

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:49.440
doing some fantastic mountains.

00:31:49.540 --> 00:31:51.540
I'll try to show you three or four different kinds of mountains

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.880
that you can do, along with the skies that you learned last time.

00:31:55.240 --> 00:31:56.120
Put these mountains in there,

00:31:56.160 --> 00:31:57.800
you've got a half-completed painting already.

00:31:58.560 --> 00:31:59.980
Alright, let's do it.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.980
And we'll take the knife here,

00:32:02.180 --> 00:32:06.560
and let's start with some Prussian blue, Van Dyke brown.

00:32:06.700 --> 00:32:08.420
These two are at about equal parts,

00:32:08.990 --> 00:32:10.730
and a touch of alizarin crimson.

00:32:10.930 --> 00:32:12.610
So we have blue, brown, and crimson.

00:32:13.910 --> 00:32:16.210
Mix it up, pull it out very flat.

00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:18.310
Let me clean the knife so you can see this well.

00:32:19.550 --> 00:32:20.550
Okay, come right up here.

00:32:21.580 --> 00:32:25.080
Now cut across this, and get a little roll of paint

00:32:25.080 --> 00:32:26.380
right on the edge of the knife.

00:32:27.030 --> 00:32:28.510
This is where the straight edge on the knife

00:32:28.510 --> 00:32:29.570
really comes in handy.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:31.780
makes the knife much, much easier to load.

00:32:31.940 --> 00:32:32.680
Alright, let's go up here.

00:32:33.840 --> 00:32:36.590
Now probably one of the simplest mountains to make,

00:32:37.160 --> 00:32:38.620
and also the most popular,

00:32:38.760 --> 00:32:40.060
is the little snow-covered mountains.

00:32:40.480 --> 00:32:42.360
Now take the knife, you have that little roll of paint

00:32:42.360 --> 00:32:45.410
on there, and push very hard, very hard.

00:32:45.590 --> 00:32:50.040
All you're trying to do here is push in a basic shape,

00:32:50.320 --> 00:32:52.520
just a very, very basic shape.

00:32:53.820 --> 00:32:55.340
The only thing that you're worried about at this point

00:32:55.340 --> 00:32:56.740
is this nice outside edge.

00:32:56.840 --> 00:32:58.630
You could care less what's happening in here.

00:32:59.260 --> 00:32:59.960
Anything can happen.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:00.960
in there, we don't care.

00:33:02.510 --> 00:33:05.880
Alright, just worried about the edge.

00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:08.640
Scrape off all the excess paint.

00:33:08.760 --> 00:33:10.880
You can probably hear how hard I'm scraping the canvas.

00:33:11.680 --> 00:33:16.660
You're not gonna hurt the canvas, really scrape it off.

00:33:17.060 --> 00:33:20.380
Okay, now one thing also to remember about mountains,

00:33:20.500 --> 00:33:21.900
if you can see the entire mountain,

00:33:22.100 --> 00:33:23.880
it's always more distinct at the top

00:33:23.880 --> 00:33:25.880
than it is at the bottom, because at the bottom

00:33:25.880 --> 00:33:27.800
we have mist, we now have pollution.

00:33:28.080 --> 00:33:29.960
These things break up and diffuse a lot.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.970
light, and cause it to look soft and misty on the bottom.

00:33:33.290 --> 00:33:35.580
Okay, so to create that effect, watch right here.

00:33:35.910 --> 00:33:40.120
Take the two inch brush, push it, bend it, and pull it.

00:33:40.740 --> 00:33:45.050
See, that's wet, and you can slide the paint on there.

00:33:45.260 --> 00:33:47.340
And automatically, it mixes with the liquid white,

00:33:47.500 --> 00:33:49.640
and you get that blended effect at the base

00:33:49.640 --> 00:33:51.460
without doing anything.

00:33:51.820 --> 00:33:53.360
Probably one of the biggest problems

00:33:53.360 --> 00:33:55.220
when putting on the base coat for a mountain

00:33:55.590 --> 00:33:58.800
is applying too much paint, very little paint.

00:34:01.080 --> 00:34:03.620
Okay, so it just, see how it just fades right into nothing?

00:34:03.760 --> 00:34:05.080
That's just what you're looking for.

00:34:06.550 --> 00:34:08.310
Okay, now let's put some highlights on there.

00:34:08.410 --> 00:34:11.200
Today, for this mountain, I'll just take,

00:34:11.320 --> 00:34:13.130
let's just take titanium white,

00:34:14.860 --> 00:34:16.500
pull it out as flat as you can get it.

00:34:16.860 --> 00:34:18.320
Just really pull it out.

00:34:18.460 --> 00:34:20.420
And once again, cut across.

00:34:20.840 --> 00:34:21.940
See that little roll of paint?

00:34:22.220 --> 00:34:24.620
There, it's very important.

00:34:25.180 --> 00:34:26.380
There, I'll turn the knife sideways

00:34:26.380 --> 00:34:27.640
so you can see how thick it is.

00:34:28.380 --> 00:34:29.960
It's most important you have that roll of paint.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.640
paint right out at the end of the blade.

00:34:31.860 --> 00:34:32.580
Okay, let's go up here.

00:34:34.280 --> 00:34:36.780
Now when you're doing this, take the point of the knife

00:34:37.360 --> 00:34:39.200
and put it at the point of the peak,

00:34:39.400 --> 00:34:40.780
or the point of your mountain up here.

00:34:40.980 --> 00:34:43.010
Touch it, no pressure.

00:34:43.780 --> 00:34:47.000
Come down the mountain and let it slowly turn

00:34:47.000 --> 00:34:49.600
so it gets wider and wider and wider as you come down.

00:34:50.650 --> 00:34:51.110
See that?

00:34:51.610 --> 00:34:53.350
And you want this paint to break.

00:34:53.590 --> 00:34:54.910
See all these little holes in here?

00:34:55.710 --> 00:34:56.870
That's what we call breaking.

00:34:57.650 --> 00:34:59.790
Alright, let me load the knife and let's go up here.

00:35:00.440 --> 00:35:01.680
and come down this peak.

00:35:03.810 --> 00:35:05.750
Just follow right down.

00:35:06.400 --> 00:35:09.250
Now you can make all kinds of little things happen here

00:35:09.250 --> 00:35:10.970
by just jiggling and wiggling the knife.

00:35:12.140 --> 00:35:13.560
Don't just pull them down straight.

00:35:13.860 --> 00:35:15.880
Put all kinds of happy little things in here.

00:35:17.890 --> 00:35:20.970
Normally I reload the knife between each and every stroke.

00:35:21.790 --> 00:35:24.170
Every time I start a new stroke, I reload the knife.

00:35:25.190 --> 00:35:26.450
Now this little peak over here,

00:35:27.200 --> 00:35:28.760
let's put a little bit of snow right there,

00:35:29.440 --> 00:35:29.960
just a tiny bit.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:31.600
a tiny bit, like that.

00:35:33.350 --> 00:35:35.590
And we can bring this down wherever you want it here.

00:35:36.120 --> 00:35:38.260
This is your mountain, so you have to make some decisions.

00:35:38.460 --> 00:35:39.480
Where's the light coming from?

00:35:40.390 --> 00:35:41.330
Notice these angles.

00:35:41.510 --> 00:35:44.110
Nearly every angle in here is going in basically

00:35:44.110 --> 00:35:45.190
the same direction.

00:35:45.530 --> 00:35:47.530
Okay, now let's mix up a shadow color for that.

00:35:48.090 --> 00:35:50.710
I'll use white, and just take a little phthalo blue.

00:35:50.810 --> 00:35:53.200
Could use white, Prussian blue, phthalo blue.

00:35:53.260 --> 00:35:55.200
Makes no difference, I'll just use phthalo blue today.

00:35:56.860 --> 00:35:58.520
Now you're looking for a color that's

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.080
darker than the highlight that you just applied,

00:36:02.320 --> 00:36:05.180
yet lighter than the base coat that's already up there.

00:36:05.960 --> 00:36:07.240
Cut you off that little roll of paint,

00:36:07.340 --> 00:36:09.260
just like before, go back up here.

00:36:09.860 --> 00:36:11.360
Now you have to make some big decisions.

00:36:11.990 --> 00:36:13.770
Which one of these peaks is in the background?

00:36:14.260 --> 00:36:16.820
Whichever one you decide, that's the one that's done first.

00:36:17.700 --> 00:36:19.320
In my mind, this little one right here

00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:21.740
is gonna be the one that's the father's back.

00:36:21.900 --> 00:36:24.010
Okay, let's go right up here, there we are.

00:36:24.810 --> 00:36:27.010
Now, do it first since it's the father's one back,

00:36:27.810 --> 00:36:29.770
and very gently lay in a little bit of highlight.

00:36:30.410 --> 00:36:31.350
or shadow, I'm sorry.

00:36:32.220 --> 00:36:34.510
Now, grab this and pull it down,

00:36:35.350 --> 00:36:37.670
and pull this one distinctly through it.

00:36:37.730 --> 00:36:39.050
That'll push that one right back.

00:36:40.750 --> 00:36:42.150
See how you can move mountains?

00:36:43.890 --> 00:36:45.470
Didn't know you had so much power, did you?

00:36:46.820 --> 00:36:49.420
You can begin building all kinds of little things in here.

00:36:50.010 --> 00:36:51.190
Each one of these little peaks

00:36:51.190 --> 00:36:53.070
needs its own individual shadow,

00:36:54.980 --> 00:36:56.640
and you can go back with highlight color

00:36:56.640 --> 00:36:59.960
and put all kinds of beautiful little things in here.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:04.250
Here, and you can put as many or as few peaks as you want,

00:37:05.600 --> 00:37:07.380
but each one needs its own shadow.

00:37:08.410 --> 00:37:10.940
In here, put a little bit of the shadow color.

00:37:11.800 --> 00:37:14.160
Notice that the shadow color is all going

00:37:14.160 --> 00:37:16.800
in basically the same angle.

00:37:17.240 --> 00:37:19.860
If you wanna show little ridges,

00:37:19.960 --> 00:37:22.120
all you do is drop in a little shadow color.

00:37:22.260 --> 00:37:24.520
You can make all kinds of little things happen in your mountain.

00:37:25.280 --> 00:37:27.200
Alright, now then, as we said earlier,

00:37:28.680 --> 00:37:29.920
we want the base of this mountain

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:33.550
to be nice and misty, so with a clean, dry brush, tap.

00:37:34.590 --> 00:37:38.850
Be very careful here that you don't tap too hard

00:37:38.850 --> 00:37:40.660
and that you follow the angles.

00:37:40.760 --> 00:37:43.320
It's most important that you follow these angles

00:37:43.320 --> 00:37:43.940
in this mountain.

00:37:44.660 --> 00:37:46.520
If you come straight across banging like that,

00:37:46.580 --> 00:37:47.560
you're just gonna cut it off.

00:37:48.040 --> 00:37:49.180
We want it very soft.

00:37:49.420 --> 00:37:50.960
We wanna be able to see through the mist

00:37:50.960 --> 00:37:52.860
and still see a little bit of detail.

00:37:53.820 --> 00:37:55.300
Over here, follow these angles.

00:37:57.030 --> 00:37:59.570
And then very lightly, holding the brush flat.

00:38:00.730 --> 00:38:02.510
Just lift upward, see there?

00:38:03.370 --> 00:38:05.970
Follow the angle still, I can't say that enough times.

00:38:06.470 --> 00:38:07.730
Very, very important.

00:38:08.470 --> 00:38:10.810
Just lift it upward, see how soft and gentle that is?

00:38:13.030 --> 00:38:13.830
Isn't that easy?

00:38:14.030 --> 00:38:16.190
You have a fantastic mountain, see?

00:38:16.410 --> 00:38:17.790
Told you mountains aren't that hard.

00:38:18.320 --> 00:38:20.940
The biggest thing is when you're putting that highlight on,

00:38:21.100 --> 00:38:23.250
is no pressure, I can't say that enough.

00:38:23.470 --> 00:38:24.850
When I was teaching my son to paint,

00:38:24.890 --> 00:38:27.470
I used to tell him to pretend if he wasn't careful,

00:38:27.610 --> 00:38:29.250
his hand would literally float away.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:31.000
It's that light of a touch.

00:38:31.160 --> 00:38:33.800
Pretend you're a whisper just floating across the canvas,

00:38:33.960 --> 00:38:34.880
and it'll work for you.

00:38:35.560 --> 00:38:36.620
Let's do a different kind of mountain.

00:38:36.940 --> 00:38:38.180
I'll use that same color.

00:38:38.420 --> 00:38:41.390
That was a Prussian blue, Van Dyke brown,

00:38:41.630 --> 00:38:42.290
a touch of crimson.

00:38:43.030 --> 00:38:44.150
Get me a little roll of paint.

00:38:44.510 --> 00:38:45.190
Okay, let's go up here.

00:38:46.010 --> 00:38:48.590
A lot of times, you want to do ridges of mountains.

00:38:50.520 --> 00:38:52.380
There's a lot of beautiful ridges.

00:38:52.520 --> 00:38:56.230
One of my favorite things to do in Alaska,

00:38:56.410 --> 00:38:58.470
and even down into British Columbia.

00:38:58.800 --> 00:38:59.980
There's a lot of ridges.

00:39:00.060 --> 00:39:02.400
which is fantastic.

00:39:06.900 --> 00:39:09.360
Once again, you start out by just really pushing

00:39:09.360 --> 00:39:10.940
that color into the fabric.

00:39:12.270 --> 00:39:15.530
Really force it in, scrape off all the excess.

00:39:16.830 --> 00:39:20.990
Then we'll take a big brush, grab it, and pull it.

00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:25.700
Once again, that causes it to be light toward the base.

00:39:27.180 --> 00:39:28.780
Helps create that misty effect.

00:39:30.440 --> 00:39:32.460
And with brush strokes, it's a nice way

00:39:32.460 --> 00:39:35.060
to lay out your entire mountain without being committed.

00:39:35.700 --> 00:39:36.600
When you're doing this at home,

00:39:36.680 --> 00:39:38.080
you'll be able to see on your canvas

00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:40.620
that each one of these brush strokes is like painting.

00:39:41.130 --> 00:39:43.350
You can see all the forms and shapes.

00:39:43.610 --> 00:39:45.870
You can move things and you go that way

00:39:45.870 --> 00:39:47.960
and you can see, you can see it there.

00:39:48.100 --> 00:39:49.720
You can create all kinds of effects

00:39:50.280 --> 00:39:51.520
just using brush strokes.

00:39:51.680 --> 00:39:54.800
It's a nice way to lay out your basic mountain shape

00:39:54.800 --> 00:39:56.250
without being committed.

00:39:57.500 --> 00:39:59.980
Alright, we'll take a little white into that.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:02.280
Now I'm gonna add a tiny touch of black.

00:40:02.820 --> 00:40:05.220
Just a tiny touch, I wanna gray this down a little bit.

00:40:06.630 --> 00:40:07.370
There we go.

00:40:09.470 --> 00:40:11.610
It's a very light color, but it's gray.

00:40:13.570 --> 00:40:16.340
Pull it out very flat, very, very flat,

00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:18.540
and the tiniest little roll of paint.

00:40:19.880 --> 00:40:21.600
Tiny roll of paint, okay, let's go up here.

00:40:22.950 --> 00:40:25.540
Now this time, hold the knife a little higher.

00:40:26.300 --> 00:40:29.880
Touch, and just let it all, just very,

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.260
barely graze the canvas.

00:40:31.520 --> 00:40:34.640
We want very, very little paint on this one.

00:40:35.820 --> 00:40:37.700
This is a little harder to do than the other mountain

00:40:37.700 --> 00:40:40.790
because it uses less paint and even less pressure.

00:40:41.210 --> 00:40:44.980
Okay, I'm gonna use, I'm gonna take some black

00:40:44.980 --> 00:40:50.280
and some Prussian blue and make a shadow color and white.

00:40:52.270 --> 00:40:55.450
So we have black, Prussian blue, little bit of white.

00:40:55.670 --> 00:40:58.060
We still want a color that's lighter

00:40:58.060 --> 00:40:59.730
than what we have on the canvas.

00:41:00.410 --> 00:41:01.920
get darker than the highlight.

00:41:03.430 --> 00:41:05.290
All right, maybe I'll add just a touch more

00:41:05.290 --> 00:41:06.090
of the blue to that.

00:41:07.100 --> 00:41:10.160
All right, good, cut us off a little roll of paint.

00:41:10.300 --> 00:41:11.100
Let's go back up here.

00:41:12.120 --> 00:41:13.700
And then we'll begin in here,

00:41:13.840 --> 00:41:17.000
just playing some of the different colors through there.

00:41:18.120 --> 00:41:19.160
I'm gonna make that a little lighter

00:41:19.160 --> 00:41:20.100
so you can see it better.

00:41:21.540 --> 00:41:23.060
I don't think it's showing up quite as well

00:41:23.060 --> 00:41:24.320
as I wanted to show for you.

00:41:25.550 --> 00:41:25.910
There.

00:41:30.700 --> 00:41:32.380
Yeah, that's showing up a little bit better.

00:41:32.620 --> 00:41:37.090
Little bit right in here.

00:41:37.190 --> 00:41:38.490
Now we just sort of play these colors.

00:41:38.570 --> 00:41:41.550
Notice these angles are all basically the same.

00:41:41.710 --> 00:41:51.820
And you just sort of go back and forth here

00:41:51.820 --> 00:41:54.880
between the highlight and the shadow colors.

00:41:56.100 --> 00:41:58.500
Very, very, very little paint.

00:41:58.790 --> 00:41:59.610
Can't say that enough.

00:42:01.180 --> 00:42:02.620
Now then, let's play some games here.

00:42:02.940 --> 00:42:07.130
You know, clean, dry brush, and I just wanna tap this,

00:42:09.260 --> 00:42:13.210
creating that soft, misty effect, and very lightly lift up,

00:42:13.310 --> 00:42:14.450
still following those angles.

00:42:16.410 --> 00:42:18.510
Light, three hairs and some air.

00:42:18.570 --> 00:42:20.330
All we're doing is caressing the canvas,

00:42:23.240 --> 00:42:24.740
just barely, barely touching.

00:42:24.840 --> 00:42:26.340
See how rocky that looks in there?

00:42:26.540 --> 00:42:26.780
Good.

00:42:27.650 --> 00:42:29.500
Now then, maybe.

00:42:30.160 --> 00:42:32.350
Maybe we can take, watch here.

00:42:32.450 --> 00:42:39.030
Let's put some right here, coming around us like this.

00:42:40.330 --> 00:42:42.030
And maybe this one comes down in front.

00:42:43.290 --> 00:42:45.290
See, you have to make big decisions here.

00:42:47.220 --> 00:42:48.550
Put a little bit right there.

00:42:51.290 --> 00:42:54.850
Very little paint and very little pressure.

00:42:55.740 --> 00:42:57.720
Though by now you're probably tired of hearing me say that.

00:43:02.140 --> 00:43:06.150
Okay, over in here, a little bit of the shadow color.

00:43:07.120 --> 00:43:08.920
Then we just pull it down and let it start

00:43:08.920 --> 00:43:12.260
blending in with the other colors.

00:43:13.090 --> 00:43:15.450
Let this paint break so some of the base color

00:43:15.450 --> 00:43:16.110
shows through.

00:43:16.410 --> 00:43:19.230
You don't want to kill all your nice base colors

00:43:19.230 --> 00:43:20.830
that you worked so hard to put in there.

00:43:24.560 --> 00:43:26.780
Just make huge, big things happening in here.

00:43:29.390 --> 00:43:29.970
Now with the shadow.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.820
shadow color, look here, if you just do that,

00:43:33.140 --> 00:43:36.000
it brings that together and creates a nice ridge

00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:37.980
right there, hmm, isn't that easy?

00:43:38.590 --> 00:43:42.250
Sneaky, I look for easy ways to paint.

00:43:45.020 --> 00:43:51.590
Got a two inch brush, and we can very gently tap that,

00:43:52.360 --> 00:43:56.560
very gently lift upward.

00:43:58.240 --> 00:43:59.960
Let's lift it upward and make it very soft.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:04.750
very far away, and that's a super way

00:44:04.750 --> 00:44:06.850
to make some of the most beautiful little mountains.

00:44:07.150 --> 00:44:09.590
And you can just keep on and on and on.

00:44:09.980 --> 00:44:12.920
You could put all kinds of little peaks within here,

00:44:13.990 --> 00:44:15.030
little things happening.

00:44:16.860 --> 00:44:18.620
You really can just get carried away

00:44:18.970 --> 00:44:24.500
and paint entire canvases, nothing but beautiful mountains.

00:44:26.270 --> 00:44:27.650
And when I was learning to paint,

00:44:28.110 --> 00:44:29.970
that was one of the things that I used to do all the time.

00:44:30.060 --> 00:44:32.910
I might paint entire big canvases like this,

00:44:33.010 --> 00:44:37.010
with nothing but layer after layer after layer of mountains.

00:44:38.140 --> 00:44:39.660
Then I had a great big putty knife

00:44:39.660 --> 00:44:41.160
used to hang beside where I worked,

00:44:41.240 --> 00:44:43.740
and then I'd take and just scrape it off and do it again.

00:44:44.620 --> 00:44:48.260
It's a lot of work, but if there's a secret to painting,

00:44:48.820 --> 00:44:49.720
it is practice.

00:44:51.700 --> 00:44:52.840
That is the secret.

00:44:54.360 --> 00:44:55.600
It's just like driving a car.

00:44:55.680 --> 00:44:56.680
You didn't jump in the car

00:44:56.680 --> 00:44:59.200
and drive it correctly the first time.

00:45:00.800 --> 00:45:01.600
you had to practice.

00:45:02.350 --> 00:45:04.250
Although I do meet some drivers sometimes

00:45:04.250 --> 00:45:07.060
that I think they only had that one lesson.

00:45:09.630 --> 00:45:15.470
So be willing to devote a little time and energy

00:45:15.470 --> 00:45:18.880
to practice, and you can create mountains,

00:45:19.480 --> 00:45:21.240
you can create total masterpieces

00:45:21.620 --> 00:45:23.330
that you didn't believe possible.

00:45:24.410 --> 00:45:27.440
