all kinds of happy little things with a round brush.

01:26:56.420 --> 01:26:58.480
Okay, one of the most popular trees.

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:00.960
is a birch tree.

01:27:01.820 --> 01:27:03.600
Let's do that, I'll take some brown,

01:27:03.720 --> 01:27:05.340
pull it out very flat, cut across.

01:27:05.660 --> 01:27:08.270
Let's go right here, we'll just make him right in here.

01:27:08.940 --> 01:27:13.200
Touch and pull, just touch and pull.

01:27:13.870 --> 01:27:15.730
Birch tree is a fun tree to make.

01:27:16.580 --> 01:27:19.160
And birch trees normally grow in clumps.

01:27:20.020 --> 01:27:23.400
So, when you're doing a birch tree,

01:27:24.270 --> 01:27:26.830
put several of them in there, don't just put one in.

01:27:26.890 --> 01:27:28.330
They normally don't stand out there by themselves.

01:27:28.650 --> 01:27:29.950
They get lonely easily.

01:27:30.000 --> 01:27:32.200
So there's always a bunch of them.

01:27:33.800 --> 01:27:35.640
And let me see here, we'll take some,

01:27:35.940 --> 01:27:38.760
we'll just use straight titanium white touch

01:27:38.760 --> 01:27:41.180
and give it a little pull, do this round.

01:27:42.470 --> 01:27:43.750
Give it a little pull, a little pull.

01:27:44.860 --> 01:27:46.910
That easy, that easy.

01:27:49.070 --> 01:27:51.890
We have a little bit of the liquid black still on the pallet.

01:27:52.860 --> 01:27:58.530
Okay, with that we can just throw in a few little tree trunks,

01:27:58.690 --> 01:27:59.730
or limbs here and there.

01:28:00.030 --> 01:28:05.650
like so, I'm gonna put leaves on these

01:28:05.650 --> 01:28:07.250
so I'm not too worried about detail.

01:28:09.520 --> 01:28:12.820
Then, then, then, I'll take a one-inch brush,

01:28:12.920 --> 01:28:14.620
or the round brush would work fine for this,

01:28:14.890 --> 01:28:16.790
and just tap it into the color, see?

01:28:17.310 --> 01:28:18.950
Instead of pulling it, I'm just tapping it.

01:28:19.960 --> 01:28:21.340
Just tap it, okay, let's go up here.

01:28:22.390 --> 01:28:25.960
And then all I wanna do is just touch, just touch,

01:28:26.310 --> 01:28:27.690
and all these happy little leaves

01:28:27.690 --> 01:28:29.210
just sort of float around out in here.

01:28:30.830 --> 01:28:33.550
They're quite loose, this is quite easy to do.

01:28:33.870 --> 01:28:38.660
You'll really enjoy, look at that, easy that is.

01:28:42.720 --> 01:28:45.350
Very loose and very airy, airy,

01:28:45.430 --> 01:28:46.650
I guess that's a proper word,

01:28:47.580 --> 01:28:48.960
means you can see some air through there.

01:28:50.440 --> 01:28:52.360
Okay, and that's basically the way we do

01:28:52.360 --> 01:28:53.820
a happy little perch tree.

01:28:54.150 --> 01:28:55.410
Let me show you one more little tree,

01:28:55.490 --> 01:28:56.610
I'm about to run out of space here.

01:28:57.580 --> 01:28:59.500
We'll just continue to use a liquid black.

01:29:00.280 --> 01:29:02.260
Now sometimes, especially in oceans,

01:29:02.600 --> 01:29:03.880
you have these little trees.

01:29:04.550 --> 01:29:08.310
Oh, it looks like somebody really, really heard them

01:29:08.310 --> 01:29:11.180
when they were little, tortured-looking little trees,

01:29:11.320 --> 01:29:14.480
because they have a rough life sitting out there

01:29:14.480 --> 01:29:15.500
next to the ocean.

01:29:15.600 --> 01:29:17.460
Boy, I mean, the wind blows through there,

01:29:17.620 --> 01:29:21.520
and salt, and all the tourists stepping on him.

01:29:22.460 --> 01:29:25.170
Boy, he has a devil of a time making a living out here.

01:29:27.240 --> 01:29:28.990
And they're very flat, and you know,

01:29:29.030 --> 01:29:29.970
sometimes they're almost...

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:33.290
They're almost so strong you could walk on them,

01:29:33.350 --> 01:29:34.170
and there's so many of them.

01:29:34.630 --> 01:29:36.890
But you need a base like that for him to stand on.

01:29:38.720 --> 01:29:39.980
Put his little arms out there.

01:29:40.860 --> 01:29:43.180
And very similar to the way that we did

01:29:43.180 --> 01:29:47.480
the big, big evergreen up there.

01:29:47.820 --> 01:29:51.490
I'll take some dark color, very similar,

01:29:52.220 --> 01:29:54.020
load it into the number three fan brush,

01:29:54.550 --> 01:29:57.280
and push, see, push upward.

01:29:59.130 --> 01:29:59.370
Go.

01:30:00.060 --> 01:30:01.500
kinds of little tops on that tree.

01:30:02.520 --> 01:30:03.940
See, they're almost flat on top.

01:30:05.300 --> 01:30:08.290
Now then, pick up a little of the yellow,

01:30:09.130 --> 01:30:11.330
and because of that dark color on there, it'll turn green.

01:30:11.800 --> 01:30:15.100
Okay, let's go back up here, just like with evergreen.

01:30:16.570 --> 01:30:19.010
We'll drop in some nice little highlights on that tree,

01:30:19.170 --> 01:30:22.380
and make him shine, like so.

01:30:25.150 --> 01:30:28.280
Now you can take down here,

01:30:28.480 --> 01:30:29.980
and just tap a little grass in this.

01:30:30.420 --> 01:30:35.010
like that, see there, that easy boy, that easy.

01:30:36.190 --> 01:30:37.310
You got a happy little thing.

01:30:38.370 --> 01:30:40.370
Okay, we're about to run out of canvas, I tell you what,

01:30:40.760 --> 01:30:42.880
I'll change canvases and I'll be back with you

01:30:42.880 --> 01:30:43.600
in just a second.

01:30:55.160 --> 01:30:56.380
Alright, welcome back.

01:30:56.620 --> 01:30:59.970
This segment of the teaching tape will be on how to

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:01.740
to do fantastic water areas.

01:31:01.800 --> 01:31:03.260
I'll show you how to do some reflections,

01:31:03.620 --> 01:31:06.240
maybe a little stream, maybe even a waterfall.

01:31:06.440 --> 01:31:08.060
Let's just start off here and see what happens.

01:31:08.750 --> 01:31:11.830
Okay, we'll start here and I'll just use a little bit of,

01:31:12.110 --> 01:31:14.470
oh, a little blue, a little brown, a little sap green.

01:31:14.710 --> 01:31:16.770
Put in some background areas here.

01:31:16.790 --> 01:31:18.270
I wanna show you how to make some reflections.

01:31:18.570 --> 01:31:19.910
So the first thing we have to do is

01:31:20.390 --> 01:31:21.880
is make something to reflect.

01:31:22.040 --> 01:31:24.000
We learned how to do trees and bushes

01:31:24.000 --> 01:31:27.040
in one of the earlier tapes, so let's just go right up here.

01:31:27.870 --> 01:31:29.970
And I'll tell you what, I like to do a little evergreen.

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:31.120
green trees, they're fun.

01:31:32.520 --> 01:31:34.000
I'll just take the one-inch brush here

01:31:34.000 --> 01:31:38.080
and just very quickly drop in some basic little shapes.

01:31:38.300 --> 01:31:40.000
I'm really not looking for a lot of detail.

01:31:40.240 --> 01:31:42.730
As I say, we've already practiced that.

01:31:42.830 --> 01:31:44.220
We got that down.

01:31:45.680 --> 01:31:47.480
While I have this brush, maybe I'll just pop in

01:31:47.480 --> 01:31:49.550
some little bushes like this.

01:31:52.610 --> 01:31:54.230
That'll give us something to reflect.

01:31:55.330 --> 01:31:57.610
Now, to paint in some water here,

01:31:57.750 --> 01:31:59.970
water is normally flat, it's normally flat.

01:32:00.000 --> 01:32:02.470
level, unless it's moving water.

01:32:03.360 --> 01:32:05.320
So I'll take a little bit of the phthalo blue,

01:32:05.540 --> 01:32:07.210
okay, let's go right up here,

01:32:08.070 --> 01:32:09.900
and I'll just pull in some water.

01:32:10.000 --> 01:32:12.420
Start at the bottom of your canvas and work up,

01:32:12.460 --> 01:32:16.170
so it gets progressively lighter toward the horizon.

01:32:17.020 --> 01:32:19.880
See, start at the bottom and work upward,

01:32:20.400 --> 01:32:22.440
and very lightly, just blend it all together.

01:32:24.150 --> 01:32:28.080
Okay, now then, I'll take another one-inch brush,

01:32:29.340 --> 01:32:29.920
and to that,

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:34.070
I'll add a little yellow and a little bit of green.

01:32:34.660 --> 01:32:37.060
I'll highlight some of these little trees

01:32:37.060 --> 01:32:38.280
and bushes we have back here.

01:32:38.460 --> 01:32:39.360
Okay, let's go up here.

01:32:40.590 --> 01:32:44.000
Just drop a little bit of highlight on there.

01:32:45.370 --> 01:32:46.590
See the other corner of the brush?

01:32:48.600 --> 01:32:53.310
We load a little paint on here,

01:32:54.000 --> 01:32:56.180
and we'll just drop some happy little colors

01:32:56.200 --> 01:32:57.540
right on these bushes.

01:33:00.220 --> 01:33:00.920
There we go.

01:33:02.120 --> 01:33:04.100
That'll give us something to reflect into the water.

01:33:04.660 --> 01:33:06.520
Now back to our brush that had the dark on it.

01:33:07.400 --> 01:33:08.340
Alright, let's go up here.

01:33:08.740 --> 01:33:11.780
Where the bush is about this high,

01:33:12.000 --> 01:33:16.240
we want to make the reflection about that high also.

01:33:16.870 --> 01:33:19.550
Now here we have a tree, so we put in the bush,

01:33:19.860 --> 01:33:20.960
and we come right down here,

01:33:21.540 --> 01:33:24.760
and we just put in a basic indication of a tree.

01:33:25.830 --> 01:33:29.810
You don't need exact duplicates, just indication.

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:31.760
This one's taller than that one,

01:33:31.940 --> 01:33:33.250
so I'll do that again.

01:33:34.140 --> 01:33:37.340
A bush right there, okay.

01:33:38.710 --> 01:33:41.050
Now with a clean, dry, two-inch brush,

01:33:41.740 --> 01:33:44.390
barely touching, grab this and pull it down.

01:33:44.610 --> 01:33:45.890
Straight down, straight down.

01:33:45.990 --> 01:33:49.600
And then go lightly across.

01:33:51.420 --> 01:33:52.420
See how easy that is?

01:33:53.960 --> 01:33:58.030
Now then, we want to reflect some of this color.

01:33:58.210 --> 01:33:59.490
So we turn the brush over.

01:34:00.000 --> 01:34:02.690
The rounded part of the brush is now pointing downward,

01:34:03.860 --> 01:34:06.700
and we very gently just reflect some of that color

01:34:06.700 --> 01:34:07.680
right into the water.

01:34:08.330 --> 01:34:10.230
Just look at the basic shapes that you have,

01:34:11.690 --> 01:34:13.550
and just drop a few of those little things in.

01:34:13.630 --> 01:34:17.120
They don't have to be exact, just the indication.

01:34:18.400 --> 01:34:20.760
Now then we find out if you really have a delicate touch.

01:34:21.620 --> 01:34:22.680
Whisper light, touch.

01:34:22.840 --> 01:34:25.740
I want to destroy, only want to diffuse.

01:34:27.380 --> 01:34:29.720
Go lightly across, lightly.

01:34:31.550 --> 01:34:34.470
See there, that's how you make those mirrored reflections.

01:34:34.670 --> 01:34:39.370
And you can push this paint, push it, see, make them wiggle.

01:34:41.190 --> 01:34:42.590
Now then, you need to make a decision

01:34:42.590 --> 01:34:45.740
where water and land meet.

01:34:45.880 --> 01:34:48.080
And there's where you'd want your dirt to be.

01:34:48.330 --> 01:34:49.490
So we'll take a little brown,

01:34:49.630 --> 01:34:51.130
cut us off a little piece like so.

01:34:51.660 --> 01:34:52.500
Let's go right up here.

01:34:53.520 --> 01:34:56.740
And into here, we can add just a little bit of land area,

01:34:58.030 --> 01:34:59.970
like so, just to show you how to do this.

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:05.940
like this, and we can take a little brown and a little white,

01:35:07.300 --> 01:35:10.220
cut us off a little roll, and go right up here.

01:35:12.080 --> 01:35:14.080
Put a little highlight on that, just so it stands out.

01:35:14.120 --> 01:35:15.060
Don't want to kill all the dark.

01:35:16.260 --> 01:35:17.180
Now with the point of the knife,

01:35:18.200 --> 01:35:19.840
cut you in a few little sticks and twigs,

01:35:23.170 --> 01:35:27.350
bring all that together, there.

01:35:28.010 --> 01:35:29.830
A few little bushes that grow right down on that.

01:35:31.440 --> 01:35:33.230
Isn't that easy, you have reflections.

01:35:33.530 --> 01:35:35.710
Now then, a little bit of the liquid white,

01:35:37.290 --> 01:35:40.560
put it on your pallet, okay, come right down here close,

01:35:40.700 --> 01:35:42.420
there we go, cut across it,

01:35:42.740 --> 01:35:43.960
so you have a little bit of paint

01:35:43.960 --> 01:35:45.720
right on the top edge of the knife, all right?

01:35:45.780 --> 01:35:51.340
Let's go up here, pushing very firmly, very firmly.

01:35:51.620 --> 01:35:55.790
Just cut in a happy little waterline, there you go.

01:35:56.930 --> 01:35:59.850
Just really, really push hard.

01:36:00.830 --> 01:36:03.210
Now this water line can go anywhere you want it to go,

01:36:03.290 --> 01:36:05.570
up, down, whatever, but it needs to remain

01:36:05.570 --> 01:36:07.050
basically straight across this way.

01:36:07.520 --> 01:36:09.380
Maybe you wanna put some little ripples on the water,

01:36:09.830 --> 01:36:10.610
just like so.

01:36:11.140 --> 01:36:14.400
They, too, need to remain basically straight.

01:36:14.780 --> 01:36:15.260
Look at there.

01:36:15.860 --> 01:36:18.640
And that easy, you have a nice little reflected area.

01:36:19.860 --> 01:36:24.460
Okay, now then, one of the most popular things to paint

01:36:24.460 --> 01:36:26.320
is happy bubbling little streams.

01:36:26.500 --> 01:36:27.540
So I'll show you how to do that.

01:36:27.800 --> 01:36:29.480
First of all, we need a dark color.

01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:31.340
We need dark in order to show light,

01:36:31.400 --> 01:36:33.040
so I'll just go into a little blue and black here

01:36:33.040 --> 01:36:34.000
with a two inch brush.

01:36:35.510 --> 01:36:37.050
Decide where your stream's gonna live.

01:36:37.840 --> 01:36:38.920
Maybe right here.

01:36:39.840 --> 01:36:42.120
And just apply a little bit of color to the canvas.

01:36:44.340 --> 01:36:44.980
There we go.

01:36:45.170 --> 01:36:47.090
I want the stream to come right around the corner.

01:36:51.510 --> 01:36:53.350
All I'm doing is applying some dark now

01:36:53.790 --> 01:36:56.560
so the light will show, okay?

01:36:57.420 --> 01:36:58.760
Now let's get the old fan brush.

01:36:59.270 --> 01:36:59.970
Fan brushes are...

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:00.640
for a lot of fun.

01:37:01.420 --> 01:37:03.400
I'm gonna dip my fan brush into the liquid white,

01:37:03.620 --> 01:37:05.960
and then go into the titanium white.

01:37:06.060 --> 01:37:08.220
I'm looking for a paint that's thinner

01:37:08.220 --> 01:37:09.200
than what's on the canvas,

01:37:10.870 --> 01:37:13.490
but not as thick as a titanium white is.

01:37:13.590 --> 01:37:14.570
Load the brush full.

01:37:14.710 --> 01:37:20.510
Here we go, all right, let's go right up here.

01:37:21.570 --> 01:37:23.270
Now, decide where your little stream starts,

01:37:23.370 --> 01:37:26.350
give it a little push, see,

01:37:26.430 --> 01:37:28.310
and begin making all those little foamy things.

01:37:28.470 --> 01:37:29.970
And you can drag it brush back and forth.

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:33.040
and just lay all kinds of pretty little highlights

01:37:33.040 --> 01:37:36.740
in the water, look at that, look at that.

01:37:38.410 --> 01:37:40.640
Now if your paint has trouble sticking,

01:37:40.860 --> 01:37:42.560
add a little more of the liquid white to it.

01:37:44.460 --> 01:37:48.360
There, see, just all these little splashes.

01:37:48.870 --> 01:37:51.230
Now in streams, you have little stones

01:37:51.230 --> 01:37:52.610
that live under the water.

01:37:53.010 --> 01:37:54.670
Maybe you can't see them, but they're there,

01:37:54.850 --> 01:37:58.170
and they cause the water to go, ploosh, look at that.

01:38:00.060 --> 01:38:01.660
It makes all those little bubbly things.

01:38:02.360 --> 01:38:04.920
And they got splashes all at the base of them.

01:38:07.440 --> 01:38:09.700
And just all kinds of beautiful little things happen.

01:38:09.920 --> 01:38:11.220
There's a, look at there, look at there.

01:38:11.460 --> 01:38:13.420
There's another one, there's another one.

01:38:13.720 --> 01:38:16.240
You can make as many of these as you want in your stream.

01:38:17.910 --> 01:38:19.590
And that's really what creates

01:38:19.590 --> 01:38:21.850
a tremendous amount of interest in the stream.

01:38:22.070 --> 01:38:22.310
Look at that.

01:38:23.230 --> 01:38:25.130
Just push these little rascals up in there.

01:38:27.680 --> 01:38:28.540
These little areas.

01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:31.940
Light against dark, dark against light.

01:38:33.460 --> 01:38:34.500
That's what makes it all.

01:38:34.700 --> 01:38:36.280
Look at that, there it is, there's another one.

01:38:36.770 --> 01:38:37.350
You knew that.

01:38:39.270 --> 01:38:43.850
Just as many or as few, just let your imagination

01:38:43.850 --> 01:38:50.740
control your stream of the liquid white.

01:38:51.830 --> 01:38:53.890
Keep it, keep it thinner than what's on the canvas.

01:39:03.000 --> 01:39:04.140
Okay, there's another one.

01:39:08.270 --> 01:39:11.420
Streams are a lot of fun, they're a lot of fun,

01:39:11.540 --> 01:39:13.910
and you really, you can really get carried away with them.

01:39:15.380 --> 01:39:17.400
Make all kinds of little things happen,

01:39:18.950 --> 01:39:19.610
and it's really fun.

01:39:19.690 --> 01:39:21.810
Put some logs hanging out in your stream sometime,

01:39:21.950 --> 01:39:23.510
and have the water churning over them,

01:39:24.810 --> 01:39:26.930
stones, and just work in layers.

01:39:27.090 --> 01:39:29.330
When you're doing the stream, start way in the back,

01:39:29.470 --> 01:39:29.970
finish it.

01:39:30.000 --> 01:39:34.500
and progressively come forward, continually come forward.

01:39:36.050 --> 01:39:37.810
Maybe down here it's getting a little bigger

01:39:37.810 --> 01:39:39.920
and you begin to see a little more detail.

01:39:40.250 --> 01:39:43.070
Just grab it, see, you can begin seeing

01:39:43.070 --> 01:39:45.590
little wave actions according to what all's happening

01:39:45.590 --> 01:39:47.810
in there, in rido now.

01:39:48.090 --> 01:39:49.590
Here's a good something to look at.

01:39:50.000 --> 01:39:52.920
See right here, we have no color on the canvas.

01:39:53.290 --> 01:39:54.010
This is light.

01:39:54.370 --> 01:39:58.160
You put light against that, see, hardly anything shows.

01:39:58.640 --> 01:39:59.820
You have to have that dark.

01:40:00.000 --> 01:40:02.260
underneath to get the contrast.

01:40:02.640 --> 01:40:04.860
If you put light against light, like right there,

01:40:05.080 --> 01:40:06.340
you have basically nothing.

01:40:07.780 --> 01:40:11.720
Alright, tell you what, one of the most popular,

01:40:12.120 --> 01:40:14.420
popular things that we do is waterfalls.

01:40:14.500 --> 01:40:15.980
I'll show you how to make a happy little waterfall.

01:40:16.870 --> 01:40:20.380
Let's take a little blue, a little phthalo green, whatever.

01:40:21.210 --> 01:40:22.330
Mainly a dark color here.

01:40:23.280 --> 01:40:26.350
And let's say, let's say our waterfall lives,

01:40:27.280 --> 01:40:29.670
shoom, right there, certainly does now.

01:40:31.400 --> 01:40:33.480
Right there, we got a happy little waterfall.

01:40:36.160 --> 01:40:37.900
And we'll just put some dark color down here,

01:40:38.020 --> 01:40:39.620
and then we'll make a decision where all this goes.

01:40:39.780 --> 01:40:43.150
We just need some dark color right now, okay?

01:40:44.070 --> 01:40:47.860
Now, let's put a few little trees into the background

01:40:47.860 --> 01:40:48.960
just to give it a little shape.

01:40:49.060 --> 01:40:50.540
I'll use the little round brush here

01:40:51.040 --> 01:40:52.620
and just tap it into some color.

01:40:53.130 --> 01:40:53.990
Okay, let's go up here.

01:40:55.010 --> 01:40:57.260
Maybe, yep, look at that.

01:40:58.370 --> 01:40:59.970
We'll just put in an indication of...

01:41:00.000 --> 01:41:01.120
a happy little tree or two,

01:41:01.220 --> 01:41:02.700
