01:56:40.830 --> 01:56:44.630
Put a little bit of color shining underneath.

01:56:45.540 --> 01:56:46.700
So I'll tell you how we'll do that.

01:56:47.280 --> 01:56:48.380
Take another fan brush.

01:56:48.600 --> 01:56:51.080
I'm gonna go right into a little bit of the cad yellow.

01:56:51.930 --> 01:56:52.990
Just get a little bit on there.

01:56:53.250 --> 01:56:53.970
Let's go right up here.

01:56:55.030 --> 01:56:56.080
Now, with this yellow,

01:56:56.650 --> 01:56:58.850
I'm gonna go right at the base of this wave.

01:57:00.000 --> 01:57:01.300
and just, oh, what a mess.

01:57:02.950 --> 01:57:04.910
Just throw in a little bit of this bright yellow.

01:57:05.110 --> 01:57:10.380
When that yellow hits the blue,

01:57:10.500 --> 01:57:12.320
it turns greenish, so we don't care.

01:57:13.180 --> 01:57:15.100
Little bit of titanium white now,

01:57:15.300 --> 01:57:17.660
right into that same color, just to brighten it up.

01:57:18.040 --> 01:57:20.770
It makes a nice yellowish green color,

01:57:20.930 --> 01:57:21.770
water-looking color.

01:57:22.800 --> 01:57:25.140
Then I'll go back to my fan brush that had the white on it,

01:57:26.930 --> 01:57:29.030
add the least little touch of phthalo blue.

01:57:30.600 --> 01:57:33.280
white, a little liquid white, titanium white,

01:57:33.460 --> 01:57:35.040
and a touch of phthalo blue.

01:57:35.450 --> 01:57:36.190
Okay, let's go up here.

01:57:37.260 --> 01:57:39.450
Now then, follow the same basic angles.

01:57:40.260 --> 01:57:42.900
Grab this, come up a little bit, over,

01:57:43.270 --> 01:57:44.370
and right into that one.

01:57:45.500 --> 01:57:47.270
Reload your brush, over.

01:57:48.540 --> 01:57:51.070
See, gotta make those little noises.

01:57:57.390 --> 01:57:59.800
See how that already, though, is looking like light.

01:58:00.220 --> 01:58:00.580
through there.

01:58:01.580 --> 01:58:05.060
It's a super easy, nice way to make that happen.

01:58:07.650 --> 01:58:11.380
Here, this is looking right straight at you.

01:58:15.620 --> 01:58:17.220
All those little things happen right there.

01:58:18.990 --> 01:58:22.340
Okay, now I tell you what, maybe the water's hitting here

01:58:22.340 --> 01:58:26.230
and it splashes back and just make,

01:58:26.660 --> 01:58:28.180
oh look at all those big splashes.

01:58:28.960 --> 01:58:29.980
Water is really.

01:58:30.000 --> 01:58:32.630
churning and hitting, that's the fun part

01:58:32.630 --> 01:58:33.450
of making these waves.

01:58:33.670 --> 01:58:37.330
I mean, you can just make that water splash and churn,

01:58:37.470 --> 01:58:39.210
it's hitting down here and splashing,

01:58:40.160 --> 01:58:42.060
all kinds of things happening.

01:58:43.520 --> 01:58:45.800
Now then, we need a reason, we need a reason here

01:58:45.800 --> 01:58:47.660
for it to be splashing up.

01:58:47.780 --> 01:58:51.110
So I'll take a little bandite brown, okay,

01:58:51.230 --> 01:58:53.650
a little roll of paint right on the edge of the knife here.

01:58:53.790 --> 01:58:54.550
Let's go right up here.

01:58:56.410 --> 01:58:58.430
Let's just put a happy little stone that lives there.

01:58:59.680 --> 01:58:59.980
I bet you.

01:59:00.000 --> 01:59:01.560
You knew there was gonna be a stone living there,

01:59:01.660 --> 01:59:05.130
didn't you, see?

01:59:05.870 --> 01:59:07.850
And maybe there's another little stone over here.

01:59:07.910 --> 01:59:10.150
Wherever you want a stone, drop it in, your stones.

01:59:11.530 --> 01:59:12.470
You put them where you want them.

01:59:13.430 --> 01:59:16.050
Little dark sienna,

01:59:17.560 --> 01:59:19.010
little highlight on some of these.

01:59:19.760 --> 01:59:22.590
Look at that, light on that one

01:59:22.590 --> 01:59:24.190
where the sun's playing through there.

01:59:26.670 --> 01:59:29.970
Okay, I'm gonna take the liquid white and take it.

01:59:30.000 --> 01:59:34.060
yellow blue again, very thin, very thin.

01:59:34.240 --> 01:59:34.980
Let's go right up here.

01:59:36.560 --> 01:59:37.880
Now there's water hitting a stone,

01:59:37.920 --> 01:59:39.400
and it's just coming over and going,

01:59:39.600 --> 01:59:40.900
oh, look at there, look at there.

01:59:42.090 --> 01:59:42.730
Isn't that super?

01:59:43.400 --> 01:59:45.540
And it comes all over, wherever you want it to go.

01:59:46.750 --> 01:59:51.130
Always water playing all through here, in here.

01:59:51.270 --> 01:59:54.640
Now then, let's splash a little bit all up in there.

01:59:56.200 --> 01:59:58.320
See, that water just goes all over the stones.

02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:03.980
Isn't that super?

02:00:04.900 --> 02:00:07.460
That really is one of the nicest, easiest ways

02:00:07.460 --> 02:00:09.560
to make a wave that's crashed over,

02:00:09.660 --> 02:00:10.400
and it's very effective.

02:00:11.040 --> 02:00:12.300
One other thing that will help,

02:00:12.680 --> 02:00:13.960
take a little bit of dark color,

02:00:15.060 --> 02:00:17.060
and right here, you need to separate this.

02:00:18.160 --> 02:00:22.940
Little bit of dark color, just enough to, see?

02:00:23.210 --> 02:00:26.480
That little line helps separate it, it's important.

02:00:30.380 --> 02:00:32.670
And we'll take a little bit of the liquid white

02:00:32.670 --> 02:00:35.120
and let's just go right in here

02:00:35.120 --> 02:00:36.520
and make some little signs,

02:00:36.800 --> 02:00:38.780
some little back and forth marks.

02:00:39.090 --> 02:00:42.470
Looks like little waves, and down in here.

02:00:44.140 --> 02:00:44.840
Isn't that easy?

02:00:45.040 --> 02:00:46.600
You have a nice wave, it's turned over.

02:00:46.820 --> 02:00:49.380
It's very effective, I think you'll enjoy it.

02:00:49.560 --> 02:00:50.840
So I'll change canvases

02:00:50.840 --> 02:00:52.560
and I'll be back with you in just a second.

02:01:03.860 --> 02:01:05.260
Alright, welcome back.

02:01:05.440 --> 02:01:08.260
This section of the tape is devoted to how to repair a painting.

02:01:08.520 --> 02:01:10.660
Of course, none of us ever make mistakes,

02:01:10.860 --> 02:01:13.080
but if you should, I hope this section of the tape

02:01:13.080 --> 02:01:16.040
will show you how to correct any problem areas that arise.

02:01:16.740 --> 02:01:19.020
Now, I've sort of, just from experience,

02:01:20.000 --> 02:01:21.660
just, I'm gonna just paint a painting here

02:01:21.660 --> 02:01:23.580
and show you the major things that happen

02:01:23.580 --> 02:01:24.960
to the majority of people.

02:01:25.500 --> 02:01:27.860
Now, I've spent years and years working in classrooms,

02:01:28.040 --> 02:01:29.980
so I think I can hit most of the big problems.

02:01:30.000 --> 02:01:35.880
problems. You may find a problem that I don't cover and hope not, but we'll try to get

02:01:35.880 --> 02:01:39.540
all of them right here. So let's start out and I'm going to act like I'm painting an entire

02:01:39.540 --> 02:01:44.580
painting here and I'll just make the major mistakes. So we're putting in the sky, let's

02:01:44.580 --> 02:01:49.360
start with that. I'll use a little phthalo blue on the two inch brush and we'll just

02:01:49.360 --> 02:01:53.220
tap in a little color. Now I'm really not trying to do a finished painting here. I'm

02:01:53.220 --> 02:01:57.430
not worried about a finished painting at all. I just want to show you some of the problem

02:01:57.430 --> 02:01:57.750
areas.

02:01:58.620 --> 02:01:58.800
Okay.

02:02:00.000 --> 02:02:01.760
I tell you what, here's a good place for a problem area.

02:02:02.020 --> 02:02:03.500
A lot of people, instead of tapping,

02:02:03.840 --> 02:02:06.380
reach up here and grab a big wad of paint on their brush.

02:02:06.480 --> 02:02:08.160
Let's go up here and I'll show you what happens.

02:02:08.770 --> 02:02:10.510
When you hit the canvas, look at that.

02:02:12.650 --> 02:02:13.410
Oh my gosh.

02:02:13.780 --> 02:02:15.440
Now, if you start out that dark,

02:02:15.620 --> 02:02:17.800
you're gonna have a sky that looks like midnight.

02:02:18.360 --> 02:02:20.040
Now, if you're doing a night scene, that's all right.

02:02:20.550 --> 02:02:21.810
But if you're doing a daytime scene,

02:02:21.890 --> 02:02:22.790
it's gonna cause you agony.

02:02:23.490 --> 02:02:25.710
If you get that much blue on your canvas,

02:02:25.850 --> 02:02:27.370
the best thing to do is stop right there

02:02:27.370 --> 02:02:28.750
and wash your brush.

02:02:30.000 --> 02:02:31.060
because it's not gonna go away,

02:02:31.310 --> 02:02:32.510
it's just gonna get worse.

02:02:33.510 --> 02:02:35.110
And very quickly, that much blue

02:02:35.110 --> 02:02:37.280
can cover an entire canvas.

02:02:39.960 --> 02:02:41.840
Dry your brush off and reload it.

02:02:42.750 --> 02:02:44.350
Pulling out a small amount of the blue

02:02:44.410 --> 02:02:46.860
and tapping the brush.

02:02:47.120 --> 02:02:49.350
Tap it very firmly, very firmly.

02:02:50.260 --> 02:02:50.960
You'll see the difference?

02:02:51.240 --> 02:02:54.520
Now this time we have a nice even distribution of color

02:02:54.520 --> 02:02:55.900
all the way across the brush.

02:02:56.210 --> 02:02:56.830
Let's go up here.

02:02:57.460 --> 02:02:59.810
Now it's very easy to add more color.

02:03:00.540 --> 02:03:02.300
It's a son of a gun, to take it off.

02:03:02.380 --> 02:03:03.740
In this case, we stopped in time,

02:03:04.100 --> 02:03:06.550
so we can just blend this until it picks up

02:03:06.550 --> 02:03:08.530
enough of the liquid white that's already on the canvas

02:03:08.530 --> 02:03:12.890
to lighten it enough that we can live with it.

02:03:13.900 --> 02:03:17.180
There we go, all right.

02:03:18.730 --> 02:03:21.810
So be very careful about how you load the brush.

02:03:22.520 --> 02:03:24.970
That's probably the first mistake that people make.

02:03:26.720 --> 02:03:28.040
Okay, add a little more color.

02:03:28.220 --> 02:03:29.960
A little bit of a...

02:03:30.000 --> 02:03:32.360
right over here, this is a 24 by 30 inch canvas,

02:03:32.560 --> 02:03:36.060
quite large, it's a lot of fun to play with.

02:03:36.440 --> 02:03:38.180
Now if you're gonna put clouds in your painting,

02:03:39.120 --> 02:03:41.740
make your sky a little darker maybe than you normally would,

02:03:41.880 --> 02:03:44.340
because you need the dark back here

02:03:44.340 --> 02:03:51.600
so your clouds will show up, okay?

02:03:52.020 --> 02:03:54.180
Now then, maybe we'll have a little water in this painting.

02:03:58.330 --> 02:03:59.970
Oh, while I have the old brush going here.

02:04:00.000 --> 02:04:03.350
I'll go right back into this phthalo blue

02:04:03.350 --> 02:04:06.270
and over here and pick up a small, small amount

02:04:06.270 --> 02:04:09.440
of the phthalo green, and just blend them together

02:04:09.440 --> 02:04:12.970
right on the brush, and let's go right down here.

02:04:13.620 --> 02:04:15.390
Now, when you're doing water,

02:04:15.510 --> 02:04:18.980
start from the bottom down here, like so,

02:04:19.210 --> 02:04:21.910
pull from the outside in, and work upward.

02:04:22.050 --> 02:04:24.700
That way, the bottom is darker than the top.

02:04:24.880 --> 02:04:28.320
Start from the bottom, and work upward.

02:04:29.110 --> 02:04:29.970
Pull from the outside,

02:04:30.560 --> 02:04:33.930
Now watch here, see, what I'm suggesting

02:04:33.930 --> 02:04:35.390
is you pull from the outside in,

02:04:35.940 --> 02:04:37.820
and leave a little area open here in the center.

02:04:37.920 --> 02:04:39.280
That'll look like a sheen of light

02:04:39.280 --> 02:04:40.800
going through your painting when it's done.

02:04:41.520 --> 02:04:43.720
Now, it's almost a natural tendency to come over here,

02:04:43.840 --> 02:04:45.740
and then turn the brush and go across.

02:04:45.900 --> 02:04:46.800
Oh, look at that.

02:04:47.560 --> 02:04:49.580
Now that's the son of a gun to blend out.

02:04:51.000 --> 02:04:52.480
And you're gonna, to blend it out,

02:04:52.560 --> 02:04:54.460
you're gonna lose this light area if you're not careful.

02:04:54.960 --> 02:04:56.840
Start from the outside and come in.

02:04:58.400 --> 02:04:59.000
There we go.

02:05:00.700 --> 02:05:03.780
outside in, and leave this little light area open.

02:05:04.490 --> 02:05:07.250
It really makes your painting very pretty.

02:05:09.220 --> 02:05:11.580
Okay, try to keep these strokes as straight as possible.

02:05:11.940 --> 02:05:14.630
Water's normally flat, normally level.

02:05:19.790 --> 02:05:21.210
See, already it gives you the impression

02:05:21.210 --> 02:05:23.800
of a little sheen of light playing through the water.

02:05:24.260 --> 02:05:24.820
That easy.

02:05:25.490 --> 02:05:27.310
And you already had the liquid white on the canvas,

02:05:27.430 --> 02:05:29.100
so it's painted, okay?

02:05:29.540 --> 02:05:29.980
Now, water's...

02:05:30.000 --> 02:05:35.140
Brush the brush, shake it off.

02:05:38.100 --> 02:05:39.560
Just beat the devil out of it.

02:05:40.140 --> 02:05:42.410
Okay, now very lightly, go all the way across.

02:05:43.500 --> 02:05:46.610
Very lightly, very lightly.

02:05:47.150 --> 02:05:48.810
See, that light area remains there.

02:05:50.950 --> 02:05:53.790
And up here, we have a clean brush now.

02:05:54.150 --> 02:05:58.120
We can blend this guy to whatever degree of softness

02:05:58.120 --> 02:05:59.480
or sharpness that we want.

02:06:01.600 --> 02:06:02.280
There we go.

02:06:03.660 --> 02:06:05.240
And don't blend it till it's dead.

02:06:05.580 --> 02:06:07.300
You can blend it till it looks like you've pulled

02:06:07.300 --> 02:06:08.640
the window shade down.

02:06:08.900 --> 02:06:10.770
And we're looking for action.

02:06:10.930 --> 02:06:12.750
See, there's light areas and dark areas

02:06:12.750 --> 02:06:14.690
and there's all kind of things happening in the sky.

02:06:16.800 --> 02:06:20.450
Alrighty, now then, let's play a little bit.

02:06:22.740 --> 02:06:25.650
Now, clouds can be made with a multitude of brushes.

02:06:26.360 --> 02:06:28.120
Maybe I'll use the one-inch brush this time,

02:06:28.180 --> 02:06:28.680
it doesn't matter.

02:06:29.200 --> 02:06:29.960
We'll take some titanium.

02:06:30.000 --> 02:06:33.660
titanium white, least little touch of the red.

02:06:34.310 --> 02:06:38.060
Least little touch, least little touch.

02:06:39.390 --> 02:06:41.980
Pull that in one direction, one direction.

02:06:42.240 --> 02:06:43.640
See, that rounds one corner.

02:06:44.420 --> 02:06:47.060
Now with a rounded corner up, we'll build a little cloud.

02:06:47.260 --> 02:06:48.020
Let's go right up here.

02:06:49.000 --> 02:06:51.290
Now, what happens a lot of times with clouds,

02:06:51.700 --> 02:06:53.790
people do this, right?

02:06:54.130 --> 02:06:56.970
See, they start here, and they'll stay in one place,

02:06:57.800 --> 02:06:58.720
and they do this.

02:07:04.220 --> 02:07:06.920
I see this over and over and over in classes.

02:07:08.810 --> 02:07:10.790
Just keep grinding away in one spot.

02:07:11.540 --> 02:07:13.540
Look at that, it just ends up being

02:07:13.540 --> 02:07:15.080
a big cotton ball up in the sky.

02:07:16.210 --> 02:07:18.410
Now, watch the difference, right beside it over here,

02:07:18.780 --> 02:07:21.730
let's put a little cloud that has some life in it.

02:07:22.740 --> 02:07:24.720
See, keep the brush moving, keep it moving,

02:07:24.880 --> 02:07:29.910
leave some areas, you want some life.

02:07:30.000 --> 02:07:31.440
in that cloud, little tiny circles.

02:07:31.910 --> 02:07:34.290
Can you see how much fluffier it is and it has some shape?

02:07:34.330 --> 02:07:35.830
It's not just a big round ball.

02:07:36.960 --> 02:07:38.460
But now, should you get one of these

02:07:38.460 --> 02:07:41.100
big cotton balls in the sky, this is how you correct it.

02:07:41.510 --> 02:07:43.390
Take your knife, go right up here,

02:07:43.770 --> 02:07:45.520
and just scrape it off.

02:07:47.460 --> 02:07:48.880
Zip it right off the canvas.

02:07:50.150 --> 02:07:53.170
Oils are so forgiving, you can do anything with them.

02:07:53.910 --> 02:07:55.490
And you can take a small amount of blue

02:07:55.490 --> 02:07:59.090
on the two inch brush and just go right back.

02:08:00.570 --> 02:08:04.140
And look-a there, just that easy, that easy.

02:08:04.600 --> 02:08:07.490
You can put your sky right back, right back in there,

02:08:07.570 --> 02:08:10.410
no problem, no problem.

02:08:12.830 --> 02:08:14.090
Very simple to correct.

02:08:14.830 --> 02:08:17.590
Now then, I'll clean that old brush off,

02:08:22.960 --> 02:08:25.290
give it a good wrap, and we're in business.

02:08:26.760 --> 02:08:29.510
Alright, now I'll go back into the titanium white

02:08:29.510 --> 02:08:29.970
with the one in.

02:08:30.060 --> 02:08:33.540
brush. Let's go right back up here and let's just bring this

02:08:33.540 --> 02:08:36.530
big old fluffy cloud right over there. See the difference?

02:08:36.790 --> 02:08:39.330
We're building some shape, we keep that brush moving.

02:08:39.820 --> 02:08:42.440
There's areas that are thick, areas that are thin, areas that

02:08:42.440 --> 02:08:46.770
have no paint at all. Look at that, see? You can take this

02:08:46.770 --> 02:08:50.600
cloud anywhere you want it to go. Now we take a clean, dry

02:08:50.600 --> 02:08:54.840
brush and here is the number one mistake when people

02:08:54.840 --> 02:08:59.080
blend clouds. Watch right here. People want to take the bottom

02:08:59.080 --> 02:08:59.640
of the brush.

02:09:01.050 --> 02:09:03.690
and they destroy, see, you can't tell

02:09:03.690 --> 02:09:05.340
where the brush is hitting,

02:09:05.520 --> 02:09:08.240
so they destroy these beautiful edges up here.

02:09:09.920 --> 02:09:11.860
There's just absolutely no way to tell

02:09:11.860 --> 02:09:14.420
where that brush is hitting if you use the bottom.

02:09:14.930 --> 02:09:16.730
Turn it up and use the top.

02:09:17.420 --> 02:09:19.300
Now let me go back and put those edges back in

02:09:19.300 --> 02:09:21.780
that got destroyed, because we want some nice,

02:09:21.800 --> 02:09:24.010
fluffy edges, see.

02:09:24.580 --> 02:09:26.540
This is how you put them back if you destroy them,

02:09:26.620 --> 02:09:29.460
just take the brush and go back and lay them in.

02:09:33.230 --> 02:09:36.770
All right, now then, very lightly.

02:09:36.990 --> 02:09:39.850
Blend just the bottom, using the top corner of the brush.

02:09:40.290 --> 02:09:41.450
Using the top of the brush,

02:09:41.550 --> 02:09:43.620
you can tell exactly where it's hitting.

02:09:44.900 --> 02:09:46.850
See there, look right there.

02:09:47.750 --> 02:09:52.900
Easy to tell where it's hitting, just like so.

02:09:53.530 --> 02:09:58.360
And you can fluff it up, fluff it, fluff it, fluff it.

02:09:59.300 --> 02:09:59.980
Big circle.

02:10:00.000 --> 02:10:03.660
strokes, and blend it very lightly.

02:10:04.040 --> 02:10:06.610
And you saved your little cloud.

02:10:08.150 --> 02:10:09.890
Now you can put as many clouds or as few

02:10:09.890 --> 02:10:11.030
as you want in your world.

02:10:11.450 --> 02:10:14.710
Maybe there's a happy little cloud that lives right here.

02:10:15.330 --> 02:10:17.140
Wherever you want them, just drop them in.

02:10:18.310 --> 02:10:19.150
Just drop them in.

02:10:20.790 --> 02:10:22.650
Clouds are one of the freest things in nature.

02:10:22.770 --> 02:10:25.030
They just play around the sky all day

02:10:25.030 --> 02:10:25.790
and have a good time.

02:10:30.990 --> 02:10:32.870
Their check comes in whether they work or not.

02:10:37.720 --> 02:10:38.720
Just fluff it up.

02:10:40.050 --> 02:10:42.030
See, you're still just using the top corner of the brush.

02:10:42.210 --> 02:10:45.460
And don't overwork it, don't overwork it.

02:10:47.000 --> 02:10:50.480
Fluff it, fluff it, give it a little blend.

