02:39:49.530 --> 02:39:51.290
touch the canvas, and bend it.

02:39:51.430 --> 02:39:52.150
Look at the difference.

02:39:52.850 --> 02:39:55.730
And begin forming this, turn it, form it.

02:39:56.220 --> 02:39:58.600
Think in your mind, there's one little bush or tree

02:39:58.600 --> 02:39:59.500
that lives right here.

02:40:00.280 --> 02:40:02.150
Each one of these are individuals.

02:40:02.910 --> 02:40:04.430
They each have personalities.

02:40:05.500 --> 02:40:09.460
Don't just do that and expect for something to happen.

02:40:10.460 --> 02:40:12.530
If you just hit it, that's what you get.

02:40:12.960 --> 02:40:15.740
Think about each one of these little fellows as a friend.

02:40:17.070 --> 02:40:19.150
See, even if you can't see them too well,

02:40:19.340 --> 02:40:20.380
make one at a time.

02:40:22.670 --> 02:40:29.070
Look there, make all these little individuals, okay?

02:40:29.270 --> 02:40:29.930
Maybe over here.

02:40:30.180 --> 02:40:33.800
Same thing, there's some happy little bushes

02:40:33.800 --> 02:40:34.780
that live right there.

02:40:36.820 --> 02:40:38.060
Reflect this into the water.

02:40:38.560 --> 02:40:40.780
Now this time you take that curve on the brush

02:40:40.780 --> 02:40:41.900
and turn it down.

02:40:42.170 --> 02:40:44.770
See it's down now, cause we're gonna tap downward.

02:40:45.320 --> 02:40:49.460
And see you get this nice leafy effect, that easy.

02:40:50.790 --> 02:40:52.980
Head on down, cause there's a tall tree there.

02:40:54.560 --> 02:40:58.800
Another tall tree, just to give us some indications.

02:41:00.410 --> 02:41:10.410
There we go, all right, now we got it.

02:41:11.100 --> 02:41:13.520
I'm gonna take, I'm gonna go back to the other side over here

02:41:13.520 --> 02:41:14.960
and I'm just gonna fill this up while I get,

02:41:15.700 --> 02:41:17.840
we'll just completely fill it up full of dark color.

02:41:18.530 --> 02:41:20.450
We're still making individuals in here though,

02:41:20.590 --> 02:41:24.000
even if you can't see them, there you can see them.

02:41:24.810 --> 02:41:27.820
See, there's still just happy little bushes living in there.

02:41:30.380 --> 02:41:36.300
Alright then, let's begin working on some detail.

02:41:36.560 --> 02:41:39.380
You know what I didn't do, that I want to do?

02:41:39.860 --> 02:41:41.420
I want to make a big tree right here,

02:41:42.010 --> 02:41:43.550
so we can have some practice with that.

02:41:43.630 --> 02:41:45.210
I'll just throw some dark color in.

02:41:45.270 --> 02:41:46.130
We know there's one there.

02:41:49.210 --> 02:41:51.430
We know there's one there, no problem.

02:41:52.760 --> 02:41:55.260
Alright, I'll take some of the dark sienna,

02:41:55.600 --> 02:41:59.570
little bit of white, pull it out.

02:42:00.060 --> 02:42:02.360
and make a little roll of paint on the knife,

02:42:02.460 --> 02:42:04.300
and we'll go up here, let's make a happy little trunk.

02:42:06.310 --> 02:42:09.010
Touch, give it a little, little pull to the side.

02:42:09.110 --> 02:42:11.620
See there, just a little pull.

02:42:13.210 --> 02:42:14.610
And as it goes down, let it get bigger.

02:42:16.700 --> 02:42:18.830
Normally, tree trunks are bigger at the bottom

02:42:18.830 --> 02:42:19.850
than they are at the top.

02:42:20.030 --> 02:42:21.550
And that's not an absolute rule,

02:42:21.650 --> 02:42:22.790
cause some trees are funny.

02:42:23.710 --> 02:42:24.950
But normally, normally.

02:42:25.440 --> 02:42:28.210
Cause sure as I say, that's the way it always is.

02:42:28.270 --> 02:42:29.230
Somebody's gonna write and tell me,

02:42:29.270 --> 02:42:29.950
well I saw a tree.

02:42:30.000 --> 02:42:34.140
back in Tucson in 1932, and there are exceptions

02:42:34.140 --> 02:42:36.720
to just about every rule in nature, but normally.

02:42:37.240 --> 02:42:49.580
Okay, go, get, see there, and that easy, that easy.

02:42:50.590 --> 02:42:52.090
We got some nice little tree trunks.

02:42:52.480 --> 02:42:56.970
All right, now then, I'll just keep using this big old

02:42:56.970 --> 02:42:59.970
two-inch brush, and we'll put a little bit of the liquid white.

02:43:00.000 --> 02:43:00.700
into the bristles.

02:43:00.900 --> 02:43:02.580
Then the paint, go into some yellow,

02:43:04.870 --> 02:43:07.770
and right into some sap green, bring it back down here.

02:43:10.250 --> 02:43:13.930
Just pull that brush back to a nice sharp chisel edge.

02:43:14.410 --> 02:43:17.500
But put the yellow in first, look how sharp it is.

02:43:18.170 --> 02:43:20.250
That way you have yellow at the bottom,

02:43:20.850 --> 02:43:22.250
and the dark color at the top.

02:43:22.470 --> 02:43:23.710
That's double loading the brush.

02:43:23.850 --> 02:43:24.730
Alright, let's go right up here.

02:43:25.480 --> 02:43:26.500
Let's do this old tree.

02:43:28.000 --> 02:43:29.920
Think about where your light's coming from in your mouth.

02:43:30.000 --> 02:43:31.900
and tells you that the light's coming from the right

02:43:31.900 --> 02:43:33.020
in this particular painting.

02:43:33.790 --> 02:43:36.210
So you want more emphasis on the right than on the left.

02:43:38.130 --> 02:43:40.620
And just tap in a few little highlights.

02:43:42.310 --> 02:43:44.240
There, don't overkill.

02:43:44.620 --> 02:43:47.180
You can very easily kill all the dark color in here.

02:43:47.380 --> 02:43:50.280
And evergreens are normally quite dark.

02:43:52.740 --> 02:43:56.160
Kill all the dark, especially toward the base of the tree.

02:43:58.730 --> 02:43:59.930
Go over to the other side here.

02:44:01.720 --> 02:44:03.120
I'll just drop in a few little things.

02:44:06.760 --> 02:44:12.760
There you go, and a few right here, see there?

02:44:13.160 --> 02:44:16.840
Don't overdo though, sometimes it starts working so nice,

02:44:16.980 --> 02:44:20.490
you get carried away and you cover up all the dark.

02:44:21.040 --> 02:44:25.480
I'm gonna wash that brush, you're ready to go.

02:44:25.620 --> 02:44:28.580
Here, shake it off, give it a good one.

02:44:30.730 --> 02:44:32.450
And we're in business.

02:44:32.930 --> 02:44:34.730
Okay, let me find a one-inch brush,

02:44:35.710 --> 02:44:37.190
go into a little bit of the liquid white,

02:44:37.410 --> 02:44:40.760
and let's begin highlighting bushes and trees here.

02:44:41.360 --> 02:44:42.920
Maybe the number one problem.

02:44:43.360 --> 02:44:45.700
Pull this brush in one direction, bend it.

02:44:45.900 --> 02:44:48.450
Keep the handle straight, see, pull it.

02:44:49.110 --> 02:44:50.730
Don't lean it over like this and load it.

02:44:50.850 --> 02:44:56.020
Straight down on the pallet and pull it one direction, okay?

02:44:56.180 --> 02:44:58.300
Let's look at the amount of paint that's on the end of that.

02:44:59.150 --> 02:44:59.850
Goodness gracious.

02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:03.300
Look at there, number one mistake is not enough paint.

02:45:03.610 --> 02:45:04.650
Okay, let's go up to the canvas.

02:45:05.850 --> 02:45:08.030
Now then, let's just play a little bit right in here.

02:45:09.590 --> 02:45:11.070
Probably the biggest thing that happens

02:45:11.700 --> 02:45:15.240
is when people first start, they'll hit this

02:45:15.240 --> 02:45:18.360
and let it slide and they get a goober like that.

02:45:19.880 --> 02:45:21.060
See, can you see that real good?

02:45:21.660 --> 02:45:22.960
Don't let it slide like that.

02:45:24.430 --> 02:45:25.850
And don't keep hitting the same area

02:45:25.850 --> 02:45:26.970
over and over and over.

02:45:31.020 --> 02:45:33.690
Look at that, that's what happens.

02:45:35.520 --> 02:45:38.530
I get photographs and questions all the time

02:45:38.620 --> 02:45:40.220
saying I'm just making mud.

02:45:40.700 --> 02:45:44.120
Okay, normally what causes mud is several things.

02:45:44.240 --> 02:45:47.480
Number one, you don't have the paint thin enough.

02:45:48.250 --> 02:45:51.670
Secondly, you don't have enough paint on the brush

02:45:51.670 --> 02:45:54.380
so you have to hit very hard to make it come off

02:45:54.380 --> 02:45:56.660
and then it smears and creates this kind of effect.

02:45:57.900 --> 02:45:59.980
The other thing is, is that you hit the

02:46:00.000 --> 02:46:02.640
Same area over and over and over.

02:46:02.800 --> 02:46:06.310
If you hit it two or three times, it's gonna turn to mud.

02:46:06.780 --> 02:46:08.780
Ideally, hit it once, okay?

02:46:09.440 --> 02:46:11.440
Now, to correct that, watch right here.

02:46:12.230 --> 02:46:14.800
Take the old knife, and you do a bushectomy.

02:46:16.340 --> 02:46:17.320
That's a bushectomy.

02:46:18.160 --> 02:46:20.860
You just zip that little rascal right off there.

02:46:21.500 --> 02:46:24.550
No problem, because this is your world.

02:46:24.630 --> 02:46:25.210
You can do anything.

02:46:26.240 --> 02:46:28.150
Now, take a little bit of the dark color,

02:46:28.320 --> 02:46:29.500
and lay it right back in.

02:46:30.000 --> 02:46:32.520
Each time you do a bushectomy or a treeectomy,

02:46:33.900 --> 02:46:35.200
it's gonna grow a little bit.

02:46:36.150 --> 02:46:37.690
Pretty soon you can turn the whole painting

02:46:37.690 --> 02:46:40.440
into nothing but trees and bushes,

02:46:40.640 --> 02:46:42.500
which is all right, that's all right.

02:46:42.640 --> 02:46:43.420
It's a good way to learn.

02:46:44.340 --> 02:46:45.720
All right, let's do it again now.

02:46:46.320 --> 02:46:47.320
Put a bit of the liquid white,

02:46:47.840 --> 02:46:48.960
run into some color,

02:46:49.200 --> 02:46:50.660
pull that brush in one direction,

02:46:51.120 --> 02:46:53.120
and that rounds one corner, see there?

02:46:54.050 --> 02:46:55.890
That rounded corner goes to the top.

02:46:56.120 --> 02:46:57.040
All right, let's go right up here.

02:46:58.010 --> 02:46:59.310
Same bush, right here.

02:47:00.320 --> 02:47:02.120
Go in, go slightly above the dark.

02:47:02.510 --> 02:47:04.070
Touch, give it a little bend.

02:47:04.420 --> 02:47:06.370
Gentle, gentle, look at that.

02:47:07.080 --> 02:47:12.290
See, gentle, easy, delicate little touch.

02:47:12.930 --> 02:47:14.550
It's a nice bush, you don't wanna hurt it.

02:47:16.160 --> 02:47:17.660
Look at there, see there?

02:47:18.360 --> 02:47:22.220
Should look like lace, just as tender.

02:47:23.320 --> 02:47:23.680
Look at there.

02:47:24.390 --> 02:47:28.680
Alright, that's the way it's done.

02:47:28.820 --> 02:47:29.560
Back up in here.

02:47:30.860 --> 02:47:32.340
I have some bushes that are a little bit darker.

02:47:32.600 --> 02:47:35.060
Now, if it doesn't stick, add a little bit more

02:47:35.060 --> 02:47:37.140
of the liquid white or even a little paint thinner.

02:47:39.310 --> 02:47:41.010
See, you could just dip your brush right

02:47:41.010 --> 02:47:44.910
into some paint thinner and then it'll stick, see?

02:47:46.010 --> 02:47:47.510
But don't try to force it to stick.

02:47:47.650 --> 02:47:52.400
It should come off your brush very easy, very easy.

02:47:52.480 --> 02:47:54.380
I'll just add a little bit of yellow ochre.

02:47:54.880 --> 02:47:56.740
We'll make this one out here really shine.

02:47:57.800 --> 02:47:59.440
Do these quite bright so you can see them.

02:48:00.640 --> 02:48:02.990
See, leave dark areas in your bush.

02:48:03.250 --> 02:48:06.000
Don't just, see them dark areas?

02:48:06.120 --> 02:48:07.000
That's what separates.

02:48:08.450 --> 02:48:10.610
If you kill all them, you got a big old flat bush.

02:48:13.710 --> 02:48:16.000
Add a touch of the bright red to it.

02:48:16.080 --> 02:48:17.960
What the heck, let's have a firecracker out here.

02:48:18.100 --> 02:48:21.930
There we go, look at that son of a gun shine.

02:48:23.190 --> 02:48:25.430
Look at there, see, and do them in layers.

02:48:25.750 --> 02:48:26.750
Do one bush at a time.

02:48:26.870 --> 02:48:28.410
We know there's gonna be a hundred bushes here.

02:48:30.440 --> 02:48:31.540
But, when you're doing it,

02:48:31.780 --> 02:48:35.780
this is the only bush in the world, only one.

02:48:36.540 --> 02:48:37.640
You're in love with this bush.

02:48:37.960 --> 02:48:44.350
Remember, he's your friend, he's your buddy, okay?

02:48:45.090 --> 02:48:47.950
Let's go up here and put a few bushes back in here.

02:48:48.090 --> 02:48:49.930
We said there was gonna be a tree back here,

02:48:50.990 --> 02:48:53.410
so I'll take a little bit of that same color

02:48:53.410 --> 02:48:54.550
I used for tree trunks,

02:48:54.590 --> 02:48:57.180
and let's just put us a happy little trunk right there.

02:48:58.240 --> 02:48:58.580
Cat.

02:49:00.190 --> 02:49:01.550
All right, and we can take the point of the knife,

02:49:01.850 --> 02:49:03.980
watch right here, see there?

02:49:04.490 --> 02:49:07.930
We just scrape in all kind of things.

02:49:08.360 --> 02:49:09.880
Now, most of this will disappear,

02:49:10.060 --> 02:49:12.030
because we're gonna cover it up with highlights.

02:49:12.290 --> 02:49:13.870
A little bit of it will show through,

02:49:14.090 --> 02:49:15.950
and people will think you work for weeks

02:49:15.950 --> 02:49:17.560
with your one-haired brush,

02:49:17.660 --> 02:49:19.280
putting all those little twigs in there.

02:49:21.340 --> 02:49:25.850
All right, let's go right up here and do this tree, okay?

02:49:26.650 --> 02:49:29.390
Trees are nothing more than bushes.

02:49:30.030 --> 02:49:30.870
that have got big.

02:49:31.780 --> 02:49:34.260
So think about it, each limb is a separate bush.

02:49:35.290 --> 02:49:37.230
So make separate entities in your tree.

02:49:38.530 --> 02:49:40.460
Look at that, see?

02:49:40.620 --> 02:49:42.940
He's got all kind of little separate things in there.

02:49:43.370 --> 02:49:45.810
That's what makes him really stand out and sparkle.

02:49:47.520 --> 02:49:49.220
Let's put one right out here.

02:49:50.860 --> 02:49:53.100
I wanna reflect those into the water, so let's do this.

02:49:53.710 --> 02:49:55.150
Decide where reflections are.

02:49:55.290 --> 02:49:57.030
They're right here, very gently.

02:49:57.460 --> 02:49:59.760
Pull straight down, straight.

02:50:00.000 --> 02:50:01.470
and just go across.

02:50:03.900 --> 02:50:05.320
Now as we do these from now on,

02:50:05.400 --> 02:50:07.500
we'll just turn the brush over and reflect them.

02:50:07.880 --> 02:50:10.340
There's a pretty one, right down into the water.

02:50:10.520 --> 02:50:13.760
See, turn the brush over, and there he is.

02:50:14.110 --> 02:50:17.970
That easy, easy, a little bit of bright red.

02:50:18.610 --> 02:50:20.310
Oh, look at that son of a gun.

02:50:21.450 --> 02:50:23.130
That makes you feel good just to look at it.

02:50:24.770 --> 02:50:26.900
Reflect him right into the water, there.

02:50:31.660 --> 02:50:34.340
See, isn't it super?

02:50:35.480 --> 02:50:37.700
Reflect that one right into the water.

02:50:37.800 --> 02:50:40.910
Turn that brush over, turn it over.

02:50:42.900 --> 02:50:44.440
Okay, there lives another one.

02:50:45.740 --> 02:50:48.060
Look at the layers, look at the layers.

02:50:48.370 --> 02:50:50.110
Layer after layer after layer.

02:50:51.480 --> 02:50:55.200
Reflect it into the water, just like that.

02:50:56.480 --> 02:50:59.960
Okay, now then, clean dry brush.

02:51:00.000 --> 02:51:02.760
Let's find out if you have a gentle touch.

02:51:03.720 --> 02:51:07.170
Barely touch, pull it down, pull it down.

02:51:07.580 --> 02:51:13.420
Lightly, lightly, lightly, and go across, just like so.

02:51:15.790 --> 02:51:18.900
Okay, now then, I'm gonna put a little bit of land here.

02:51:21.080 --> 02:51:24.500
Just use some Van Dyke Brown, there.

02:51:25.080 --> 02:51:26.680
Just follow the angles,

02:51:26.900 --> 02:51:29.120
so think of the lay of the land hat comes down here.

02:51:29.300 --> 02:51:29.980
And follow.

02:51:30.000 --> 02:51:30.680
Follow those angles.

02:51:31.500 --> 02:51:33.040
Don't just throw these in at random.

02:51:34.080 --> 02:51:36.620
Think about it, think about it.

02:51:37.780 --> 02:51:40.200
You know, water is normally in a recessed area.

02:51:40.780 --> 02:51:42.100
It doesn't stay on top of the mountain.

02:51:42.200 --> 02:51:43.180
It goes down in the bottom,

02:51:43.660 --> 02:51:45.240
unless there's a hole in the top of the mountain.

02:51:46.760 --> 02:51:48.440
So think about the angles here.

02:51:48.900 --> 02:51:51.440
Now, let's use a very light color so you can see it.

02:51:51.950 --> 02:51:55.100
Here's another major mistake that I see quite frequently.

02:51:56.140 --> 02:51:57.720
People will put the land in here.

02:51:57.780 --> 02:51:58.280
Come right here.

02:51:58.660 --> 02:51:59.900
Instead of following that angle,

02:52:00.090 --> 02:52:03.530
They'll come straight down and look in there.

02:52:04.080 --> 02:52:06.100
That don't look right, you just made cliffs.

02:52:07.600 --> 02:52:10.070
Your tree's gonna fall off in the water, alright?

02:52:10.210 --> 02:52:11.290
We'll just zip that right off.

02:52:11.470 --> 02:52:14.770
We'll do a landectomy this time.

02:52:16.550 --> 02:52:18.670
Let's go back and lay in a dark color.

02:52:18.750 --> 02:52:20.010
You need a dark so the light will show.

02:52:22.300 --> 02:52:23.360
Now pick up the highlight.

02:52:24.030 --> 02:52:24.850
Look at the difference.

02:52:25.240 --> 02:52:28.350
Follow these angles and don't kill all the darks.

02:52:28.610 --> 02:52:29.810
See, let the paint break.

02:52:30.960 --> 02:52:32.900
Let it break, let it break.

02:52:33.340 --> 02:52:35.190
Gentle touch, like that.

02:52:35.370 --> 02:52:36.010
See what a difference?

02:52:36.910 --> 02:52:38.990
That flows more and it looks better.

02:52:39.250 --> 02:52:41.280
It really follows the lay of the land.

02:52:41.540 --> 02:52:44.060
Take a little bit of the liquid white,

02:52:44.240 --> 02:52:48.540
go right up here, and drop us in a happy little water line.

02:52:49.700 --> 02:52:50.720
Just like so.

02:52:53.720 --> 02:52:58.140
Just cut it in, use a lot of pressure, like that.

02:53:00.160 --> 02:53:04.350
Okay, now then, let me find a one-inch brush.

02:53:04.730 --> 02:53:07.490
See, now right in here, these edges are very sharp.

02:53:07.630 --> 02:53:08.270
They bother me.

02:53:08.740 --> 02:53:10.860
So if you take this brush and just use it sidewards,

02:53:10.980 --> 02:53:14.360
push up, see, you can bring little grassy areas right down,

02:53:15.340 --> 02:53:16.940
kill that edge, bring it all together.

02:53:17.460 --> 02:53:19.740
Then we'll take the knife and scrape in

02:53:19.740 --> 02:53:21.160
some little sticks and twigs.

02:53:21.300 --> 02:53:26.350
Look at there, see, couple over here, wherever you want.

02:53:27.180 --> 02:53:29.060
All right, now this tree up here,

02:53:29.160 --> 02:53:29.960
I'm gonna put some little...

02:53:30.190 --> 02:53:31.090
dead twigs on it.

02:53:31.900 --> 02:53:34.970
So just take the point of the knife, pull some out.

02:53:35.070 --> 02:53:35.550
That simple.

02:53:35.770 --> 02:53:37.110
Let's go back over to the other side.

02:53:38.030 --> 02:53:40.090
These little grassy areas we were talking about,

02:53:40.850 --> 02:53:43.240
watch here, let's put another bush right here real quick.

02:53:45.910 --> 02:53:46.610
Son of a gun.

02:53:49.880 --> 02:53:52.080
Now when you can get your bushes to look like that,

02:53:52.320 --> 02:53:55.660
oh, you're gonna be so happy, so happy.

02:53:56.400 --> 02:53:58.220
Watch, make grassy areas.

02:53:58.300 --> 02:53:59.510
Take the brush, push.

02:54:00.030 --> 02:54:01.380
and bend it upward, see?

02:54:02.330 --> 02:54:04.720
And do this in layers, layer after layer.

02:54:04.920 --> 02:54:07.720
And this helps create the flow of the land,

02:54:07.820 --> 02:54:08.540
the lay of the land.

02:54:09.050 --> 02:54:10.110
See what's happening already?

02:54:10.230 --> 02:54:11.690
Let's go all the way down here, watch here.

02:54:14.110 --> 02:54:15.790
Look at that, look at that.

02:54:16.110 --> 02:54:19.770
See, you can adjust one loading of the brush,

02:54:19.950 --> 02:54:21.830
you can make a whole meadow right there.

02:54:22.800 --> 02:54:23.740
See there, what's happening?

02:54:24.300 --> 02:54:26.040
And it creates depth in your painting.

02:54:26.780 --> 02:54:29.060
Shoot, you can get carried away and just fill it all up.

02:54:30.510 --> 02:54:31.810
Okay, let me load a little more color.

02:54:32.190 --> 02:54:34.790
Let's put a happy little bush right there.

02:54:38.160 --> 02:54:40.320
This bush will help push everything back.

02:54:41.230 --> 02:54:42.690
Work in layers, work in layers.

02:54:43.990 --> 02:54:48.950
Maybe right here lives a happy little stone.

02:54:51.270 --> 02:54:53.670
Yeah, now when you're highlighting this stone,

02:54:53.850 --> 02:54:55.670
if you have mountains, your mountain will tell you

02:54:55.670 --> 02:54:57.880
in which direction the light cometh.

02:55:00.320 --> 02:55:05.100
So, you highlight it just like you do a mountain.

02:55:06.460 --> 02:55:08.480
Stones are just little baby mountains

02:55:08.480 --> 02:55:10.360
that haven't grown up yet.

02:55:10.560 --> 02:55:19.560
We go right in here with a little more color,

02:55:19.720 --> 02:55:21.730
and we wanna put some grass around his foots.

02:55:22.060 --> 02:55:23.640
That pushes him down into the painting.

02:55:24.700 --> 02:55:25.380
That easy.

02:55:28.670 --> 02:55:28.970
You know,

02:55:30.030 --> 02:55:31.630
I didn't mean to do a whole painting here,

02:55:31.690 --> 02:55:33.550
I was just gonna show you a few correction areas.

02:55:34.490 --> 02:55:36.130
But since we did, what the heck.

02:55:36.990 --> 02:55:38.790
Scratch in a few little sticks and twigs,

02:55:39.690 --> 02:55:41.680
few little dead things on these evergreens.

02:55:41.760 --> 02:55:45.150
Evergreens always have these, so drop a few of them in.

02:55:45.290 --> 02:55:46.590
They make it look better.

02:55:48.620 --> 02:55:50.500
And these sticks go in the dark areas.

02:55:51.410 --> 02:55:53.710
Put them in the dark areas, not on the bright areas.

02:55:58.060 --> 02:55:59.730
Let's take the liner brush.

02:56:00.190 --> 02:56:01.350
I'll use a little paint thinner

02:56:01.350 --> 02:56:03.930
and go into some Van Dyke Brown.

02:56:05.120 --> 02:56:07.120
Then is water, then is water.

02:56:07.240 --> 02:56:07.960
Let's go right up here.

02:56:09.350 --> 02:56:11.310
Maybe a little stick that lives right here.

02:56:11.910 --> 02:56:14.160
Choo, wiggle these.

02:56:15.840 --> 02:56:16.880
Just give them a little wiggle.

02:56:18.530 --> 02:56:19.870
This old dead stick will lay in here.

02:56:21.630 --> 02:56:23.190
Put some little arms on him, whatever.

02:56:27.980 --> 02:56:28.160
Ready.

02:56:30.000 --> 02:56:34.440
I think we are to the point where we have a finished tape.

02:56:36.180 --> 02:56:38.440
If you've enjoyed this instructional videotape,

02:56:39.780 --> 02:56:41.200
we have all kinds of tapes

02:56:41.200 --> 02:56:43.640
by many, many different artists, not just myself.

02:56:44.260 --> 02:56:46.620
We have people that do all of the different mediums

02:56:46.620 --> 02:56:49.550
and some of the most beautiful paintings you've ever seen.

02:56:49.810 --> 02:56:52.730
If you'd like a free catalog, drop us a line at the address

02:56:52.730 --> 02:56:53.970
that you see at the end of the show,

02:56:54.130 --> 02:56:55.910
and we'd be glad to send you one.

02:56:56.740 --> 02:56:59.000
And let us know what you'd like to see in future shows,

02:56:59.020 --> 02:56:59.980
if there's something that...

02:57:00.350 --> 02:57:02.270
you want to learn how to do that we're not teaching you,

02:57:02.510 --> 02:57:03.350
drop me a line.

02:57:03.530 --> 02:57:04.870
If I can't do it, shoot,

02:57:05.010 --> 02:57:06.310
I'll go out and find somebody that can.

02:57:07.510 --> 02:57:08.750
Okay, I'm ready to sign this one.

02:57:09.310 --> 02:57:10.850
To sign it, I use a thin oil,

02:57:11.030 --> 02:57:16.300
go right into the red, turn that, turn it.

02:57:17.650 --> 02:57:19.680
Okay, let's go right up here.

02:57:19.950 --> 02:57:21.130
We'll sign it right here today.

02:57:23.730 --> 02:57:25.130
And I really thank you for joining me

02:57:25.130 --> 02:57:28.040
for this instructional videotape.

02:57:28.490 --> 02:57:29.410
Hope it has taught you.

02:57:30.350 --> 02:57:31.210
a great deal.

02:57:32.140 --> 02:57:33.460
I have enjoyed being with you,

02:57:33.580 --> 02:57:36.360
and I hope we paint again together

02:57:36.360 --> 02:57:37.700
many times in the future,

02:57:38.640 --> 02:57:40.960
and from all of us, at the Joy of Painting,

02:57:41.610 --> 02:57:43.310
I'd like to wish you happy painting,

02:57:44.200 --> 02:57:45.620
God bless, and we'll see you again.
